msgstr "-2 體力"

msgctxt "woh_nana:516"
msgid "-2 REASON"
msgstr "-2 理智"

msgctxt "woh_nana:517"
msgid "+5% DOOM"
msgstr "+5% 末日"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:518"
msgid "SALT-DRIED EYES"
msgstr "鹽乾的眼睛"

#. Descripción de «SALT-DRIED EYES» (woh_nana:518).
msgctxt "woh_nana:519"
msgid ""
"[your eyes burn and crust over with a thin layer of salt, making the world blur]\n"
"-1 PERCEPTION"
msgstr ""
"[雙眼感到灼熱，並被一層薄薄的鹽給覆蓋，使你眼前的世界變得模糊。]\n"
"-1 感知"

#. Opción de «SALT-DRIED EYES» (woh_nana:518). Opciones: <<is it an infection?>> · HOLLOWED VEIN.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:520"
msgid "<<is it an infection?>>"
msgstr "「我是被感染了嗎？」"

#. Opción de «SALT-DRIED EYES» (woh_nana:518). Opciones: <<is it an infection?>> · HOLLOWED VEIN.
msgctxt "woh_nana:521"
msgid "HOLLOWED VEIN"
msgstr "中空的血管"

#. Parte de «SALT-DRIED EYES» (woh_nana:518).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:522"
msgid ""
"[a vein on your arm collapses inward, forming a thin channel that feels >>empty<<, as if the blood avoids flowing through it]\n"
"-2 MAX STAMINA"
msgstr ""
"[手臂上一條靜脈向內塌陷，形成一條細而中空的通道，感覺「空無一物」，彷彿血液刻意不流向該處]\n"
"-2 體力上限"

#. Parte de «SALT-DRIED EYES» (woh_nana:518).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:523"
msgid "<<it doesn't hurt>>"
msgstr "「這不會痛」"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:524"
msgid "WEIRD BRUISE"
msgstr "詭異瘀青"

#. Descripción de «WEIRD BRUISE» (woh_nana:524).
msgctxt "woh_nana:525"
msgid ""
"[the dark bruise on your ribs feels strangely soft, as if the bone beneath is dissolving]\n"
"-1 STAMINA"
msgstr ""
"[肋骨上的深色瘀青感覺異常柔軟，彷彿底下的骨頭正在被溶解]\n"
"-1 體力"

#. Opción de «WEIRD BRUISE» (woh_nana:524). Opciones: <<something's growing>> · MISALIGNED VISION.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:526"
msgid "<<something's growing>>"
msgstr "「有什麼在生長著」"

#. Opción de «WEIRD BRUISE» (woh_nana:524). Opciones: <<something's growing>> · MISALIGNED VISION.
msgctxt "woh_nana:527"
msgid "MISALIGNED VISION"
msgstr "複視"

#. Parte de «WEIRD BRUISE» (woh_nana:524).
msgctxt "woh_nana:528"
msgid "PREPARE YOUR ATTACK and ATTACK BOOST combat actions take longer"
msgstr "戰鬥行動「準備攻擊」和「攻擊加成」的所需時間增加"

#. Parte de «WEIRD BRUISE» (woh_nana:524).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:529"
msgid "<<nauseating double-image>>"
msgstr "「令人作嘔的重影」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:530"
msgid "BITE MARKS"
msgstr "咬痕"

msgctxt "woh_nana:531"
msgid "every enemy attack adds -1 STAMINA penalty"
msgstr "所有敵人的攻擊附帶 -1 體力的懲罰"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:532"
msgid "<<it hurts like hell>>"
msgstr "「痛得要命」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:533"
msgid "MELANCHOLIA"
msgstr "憂鬱症"

msgctxt "woh_nana:534"
msgid "-2 REASON after completing each mystery"
msgstr "解開謎團時 -2 理智"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:535"
msgid "<<it's hopeless!>>"
msgstr "「一切都沒救了！」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:536"
msgid "PRIMAL FEAR"
msgstr "原始恐懼"

msgctxt "woh_nana:537"
msgid "-2 STAMINA after completing each mystery"
msgstr "解開謎團時 -2 體力"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:538"
msgid "<<it can't be...>>"
msgstr "「怎麼可能……」"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:539"
msgid "TIRED"
msgstr "疲勞"

#. Descripción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539).
msgctxt "woh_nana:540"
msgid ""
"-1 to all stats until the end of the mystery\n"
"REST additional action removes it"
msgstr ""
"當前謎團結束前，所有數值 -1\n"
"進行休息的額外行動能移除此狀態"

#. Opción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539). Opciones: <<...yawn...>> · UNDER-PREPARED · -1 to all stats for all event skill checks · <<I should've brought it>> · AT A CROSSROADS.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:541"
msgid "<<...yawn...>>"
msgstr "「好想睡……」"

#. Opción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539). Opciones: <<...yawn...>> · UNDER-PREPARED · -1 to all stats for all event skill checks · <<I should've brought it>> · AT A CROSSROADS.
msgctxt "woh_nana:542"
msgid "UNDER-PREPARED"
msgstr "怠惰"

#. Opción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539). Opciones: <<...yawn...>> · UNDER-PREPARED · -1 to all stats for all event skill checks · <<I should've brought it>> · AT A CROSSROADS.
msgctxt "woh_nana:543"
msgid "-1 to all stats for all event skill checks"
msgstr "遭遇事件能力檢測時，所有數值 -1"

#. Opción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539). Opciones: <<...yawn...>> · UNDER-PREPARED · -1 to all stats for all event skill checks · <<I should've brought it>> · AT A CROSSROADS.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:544"
msgid "<<I should've brought it>>"
msgstr "「應該事前做好準備的……」"

#. Opción de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539). Opciones: <<...yawn...>> · UNDER-PREPARED · -1 to all stats for all event skill checks · <<I should've brought it>> · AT A CROSSROADS.
msgctxt "woh_nana:545"
msgid "AT A CROSSROADS"
msgstr "十字路口前"

#. Parte de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539).
msgctxt "woh_nana:546"
msgid ""
"+5% DOOM\n"
"\n"
"to remove this curse:\n"
"(use): -3 STAMINA\n"
"(discard): -3 REASON"
msgstr ""
"+5% 末日\n"
"\n"
"移除此詛咒：\n"
"（使用）：-3 體力\n"
"（丟棄）：-3 理智"

#. Parte de «TIRED» (woh_nana:539).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:547"
msgid "<<Just sign here>>"
msgstr "「請在此簽名」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:548"
msgid "JUNPEI'S NOTEBOOK"
msgstr "純平的筆記本"

msgctxt "woh_nana:549"
msgid "+1 to all STATS"
msgstr "所有數值 +1"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:550"
msgid "<<he's gone>>"
msgstr "「他不見了」"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:551"
msgid "<<My dear friend...>>"
msgstr "「我的好友……」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:552"
msgid "HITOMI'S JACKET"
msgstr "仁美的外套"

msgctxt "woh_nana:553"
msgid "+1 DAMAGE"
msgstr "造成的傷害 +1"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:554"
msgid "<<she's gone>>"
msgstr "「她不見了」"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:555"
msgid "HOLLOWED HIKER"
msgstr "空洞登山客"

#. Descripción de «HOLLOWED HIKER» (woh_nana:555).
msgctxt "woh_nana:556"
msgid ""
"Following a trail, you spot someone waving at you from the slope ahead. When you approach, you realize their face is… hollow.\n"
"\n"
"Yet there’s no panic to their movements, like this is just something they've done again and again..."
msgstr ""
"你在山路上走著走著，看見有人在前方的斜坡朝你揮手。\n"
"當你靠近時，才發現他的臉……是中空的。\n"
"\n"
"但他卻一點都不驚慌，彷彿這已經是他日常的一部分……"

#. Parte de «HOLLOWED HIKER» (woh_nana:555).
msgctxt "woh_nana:557"
msgid "A hiker who encountered something evil in the fog. They now wander, trying to remember who they were."
msgstr "在霧中遭遇某種邪惡之物的登山客。他現在四處遊蕩，想努力回憶起自己是誰。"

#. Parte de «HOLLOWED HIKER» (woh_nana:555).
msgctxt "woh_nana:558"
msgid "The HOLLOWED HIKER swings a rusted knife!"
msgstr "空洞登山客揮出了生鏽的小刀！"

#. Parte de «HOLLOWED HIKER» (woh_nana:555).
msgctxt "woh_nana:559"
msgid "The HOLLOWED HIKER stumbles towards you!"
msgstr "空洞登山客朝你蹣跚地走來！"

#. Parte de «HOLLOWED HIKER» (woh_nana:555).
msgctxt "woh_nana:560"
msgid "The HOLLOWED HIKER claws at your face!"
msgstr "空洞登山客往你臉上抓了過去！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:561"
msgid "SKINNY MONK"
msgstr "嶙峋消瘦的僧侶"

#. Descripción de «SKINNY MONK» (woh_nana:561).
msgctxt "woh_nana:562"
msgid ""
"You find a shrine tucked into the rock wall, spotting an emaciated figure sitting in stillness. Unsure if that’s just a statue, you take a step back.\n"
"\n"
"The figure rises up and points his crooked finger at you."
msgstr ""
"你在岩壁中發現一座小寺廟，而有個枯槁的身影在那裡靜靜坐著。你不確定那是否是一尊雕像，便往後退了一步。\n"
"\n"
"那道身影隨即站了起來，用他扭曲的手指指著你。"

#. Parte de «SKINNY MONK» (woh_nana:561).
msgctxt "woh_nana:563"
msgid "A monk who starved himself to glimpse the other side. Now, he seeks to consume others to preserve his vision."
msgstr "為了窺探來世而絕食的僧侶。現在，他打算消化他人以保存這個視角。"

#. Parte de «SKINNY MONK» (woh_nana:561).
msgctxt "woh_nana:564"
msgid "SKINNY MONK lunges forward!"
msgstr "消瘦僧侶朝你衝了過來！"

#. Parte de «SKINNY MONK» (woh_nana:561).
msgctxt "woh_nana:565"
msgid "SKINNY MONK bites your arm!"
msgstr "消瘦僧侶咬你的手臂！"

#. Parte de «SKINNY MONK» (woh_nana:561).
msgctxt "woh_nana:566"
msgid "SKINNY MONK chants with bleeding gums!"
msgstr "消瘦僧侶露出流血的牙齦開始唸咒！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:567"
msgid "MOUTHS IN THE MIST"
msgstr "霧中之嘴"

#. Descripción de «MOUTHS IN THE MIST» (woh_nana:567).
msgctxt "woh_nana:568"
msgid ""
"The mist rolls in too fast to be natural.\n"
"\n"
"The whispers grow hungry…"
msgstr ""
"濃霧湧入的速度快到很不自然。\n"
"\n"
"低語聲變得飢餓……"

#. Parte de «MOUTHS IN THE MIST» (woh_nana:567).
msgctxt "woh_nana:569"
msgid "Teeth, tongues, and endless mouths drift in the fog, whispering in dead languages."
msgstr "牙齒、舌頭和無數的嘴漂浮在霧中，用滅絕的語言低聲呢喃著。"

#. Parte de «MOUTHS IN THE MIST» (woh_nana:567).
msgctxt "woh_nana:570"
msgid "MOUTHS IN THE MIST lash your leg!"
msgstr "霧中之嘴攻擊你的腳！"

#. Parte de «MOUTHS IN THE MIST» (woh_nana:567).
msgctxt "woh_nana:571"
msgid "MOUTHS IN THE MIST bite into your shoulder!"
msgstr "霧中之嘴啃咬你的肩膀！"

#. Parte de «MOUTHS IN THE MIST» (woh_nana:567).
msgctxt "woh_nana:572"
msgid "MOUTHS IN THE MIST whisper nonsense!"
msgstr "霧中之嘴在小聲說著無意義的語言！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:573"
msgid "TREE-BEARER"
msgstr "負樹者"

#. Descripción de «TREE-BEARER» (woh_nana:573).
msgctxt "woh_nana:574"
msgid ""
"You spot a figure slowly climbing up the path. A whole tree is growing out of their back.\n"
"With each step they take, you grow weaker…"
msgstr ""
"你瞧見某個身影在路上緩慢爬行著。\n"
"有一整棵樹長在他的背上。\n"
"他每走一步，你就變得更加虛弱……"

#. Parte de «TREE-BEARER» (woh_nana:573).
msgctxt "woh_nana:575"
msgid "A villager, cursed to carry the sacred tree up the mountain for eternity."
msgstr "因受到詛咒而得永世搬運聖樹的村民。"

#. Parte de «TREE-BEARER» (woh_nana:573).
msgctxt "woh_nana:576"
msgid "TREE-BEARER mutters an old prayer!"
msgstr "負樹者小聲唸出古老的禱文！"

#. Parte de «TREE-BEARER» (woh_nana:573).
msgctxt "woh_nana:577"
msgid "TREE-BEARER swings a club at you!"
msgstr "負樹者朝你揮出棍子！"

#. Parte de «TREE-BEARER» (woh_nana:573).
msgctxt "woh_nana:578"
msgid "TREE-BEARER attacks you!"
msgstr "負樹者攻擊你！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:579"
msgid "SPINAL CENTIPEDE"
msgstr "脊椎蜈蚣"

#. Descripción de «SPINAL CENTIPEDE» (woh_nana:579).
msgctxt "woh_nana:580"
msgid "Something long and bone-white scurries past your leg, causing you to trip. As you try to get up, the thing slithers upright. It twitches, as if deciding whether your own spine will fit in."
msgstr ""
"某個長而慘白的東西從你的腿邊竄過，將你給絆倒。\n"
"當你準備站起身時，那東西也開始扭動並立了起來。\n"
"牠抽搐著，彷彿在思考你的脊椎適不適合放進自己的身體裡。"

#. Parte de «SPINAL CENTIPEDE» (woh_nana:579).
msgctxt "woh_nana:581"
msgid "Made from the fused spines of unlucky victims, it’s looking for a new donor."
msgstr "由不幸的受害者的脊椎所組成。牠正在尋找新的捐贈者。"

#. Parte de «SPINAL CENTIPEDE» (woh_nana:579).
msgctxt "woh_nana:582"
msgid "SPINAL CENTIPEDE writhes toward you!"
msgstr "脊椎蜈蚣朝你爬了過來！"

#. Parte de «SPINAL CENTIPEDE» (woh_nana:579).
msgctxt "woh_nana:583"
msgid "SPINAL CENTIPEDE slashes your shins!"
msgstr "脊椎蜈蚣砍你的脛骨！"

#. Parte de «SPINAL CENTIPEDE» (woh_nana:579).
msgctxt "woh_nana:584"
msgid "You feel something pulling on your spine!"
msgstr "你覺得有東西在拉扯你的脊椎！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:585"
msgid "BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER"
msgstr "黑板尖叫者"

#. Descripción de «BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER» (woh_nana:585).
msgctxt "woh_nana:586"
msgid ""
"When you step into an empty classroom, the blackboard begins to screech violently, revealing a thin figure crawling out of it.\n"
"\n"
"Your ears begin to ring…\n"
"no, they begin to bleed."
msgstr ""
"當你走進空教室時，黑板發出了刺耳的摩擦聲，有道瘦弱的身影也從中爬了出來。\n"
"\n"
"你開始耳鳴……\n"
"不對，耳朵開始流血了。"

#. Parte de «BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER» (woh_nana:585).
msgctxt "woh_nana:587"
msgid "An angry spirit of a bullied student, trapped between chalk lines."
msgstr "一名遭霸凌的學生，最終成為怨靈，受困於粉筆線條之間。"

#. Parte de «BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER» (woh_nana:585).
msgctxt "woh_nana:588"
msgid "BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER screams painfully!"
msgstr "黑板尖叫者痛苦地吶喊著！"

#. Parte de «BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER» (woh_nana:585).
msgctxt "woh_nana:589"
msgid "A piece of chalk explodes in your mouth!"
msgstr "粉筆在你嘴裡炸開！"

#. Parte de «BLACKBOARD SHRIEKER» (woh_nana:585).
msgctxt "woh_nana:590"
msgid "Your name appears on the blackboard!"
msgstr "你的名字出現在黑板上！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:591"
msgid "CEILING CRAWLER"
msgstr "天花板爬行者"

#. Descripción de «CEILING CRAWLER» (woh_nana:591).
msgctxt "woh_nana:592"
msgid ""
"Something’s making noise in the apartment above again.\n"
"\n"
"But when you look up, it’s already staring back…"
msgstr ""
"公寓上方又傳出了噪音。\n"
"\n"
"當你往上看的時候，你發現那東西早就在看著你……"

#. Parte de «CEILING CRAWLER» (woh_nana:591).
msgctxt "woh_nana:593"
msgid "A former tenant who refused to ever leave, even after death."
msgstr "一直到死後都還不願離開的前租客。"

#. Parte de «CEILING CRAWLER» (woh_nana:591).
msgctxt "woh_nana:594"
msgid "CEILING CRAWLER drops on your back!"
msgstr "天花板爬行者掉到你的背上！"

#. Parte de «CEILING CRAWLER» (woh_nana:591).
msgctxt "woh_nana:595"
msgid "CEILING CRAWLER grabs you by your hair!"
msgstr "天花板爬行者開始猛抓你的頭髮！"

#. Parte de «CEILING CRAWLER» (woh_nana:591).
msgctxt "woh_nana:596"
msgid "CEILING CRAWLER slashes you!"
msgstr "天花板爬行者砍你！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:597"
msgid "WARD ORDERLY"
msgstr "病院助理"

#. Descripción de «WARD ORDERLY» (woh_nana:597).
msgctxt "woh_nana:598"
msgid "The figure at the end of a hallway drags a blood-slicked bed frame behind him, humming a lullaby hopelessly out of tune."
msgstr "走廊盡頭的身影拖著一副沾滿鮮血的床架。他口中還哼著完全走音、聽來極其荒腔走板的搖籃曲。"

#. Parte de «WARD ORDERLY» (woh_nana:597).
msgctxt "woh_nana:599"
msgid "A former night-shift worker who vanished months ago."
msgstr "一個月前消失的前夜班員工。"

#. Parte de «WARD ORDERLY» (woh_nana:597).
msgctxt "woh_nana:600"
msgid "WARD ORDERLY jabs you with an old syringe!"
msgstr "病院助理拿老舊的注射器戳你！"

#. Parte de «WARD ORDERLY» (woh_nana:597).
msgctxt "woh_nana:601"
msgid "WARD ORDERLY grabs your neck!"
msgstr "病院助理掐住你的脖子！"

#. Parte de «WARD ORDERLY» (woh_nana:597).
msgctxt "woh_nana:602"
msgid "WARD ORDERLY hits you with a dirty bedpan!"
msgstr "病院助理拿骯髒的便盆打你！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:603"
msgid "BARNACLE BLOOM"
msgstr "藤壺花"

#. Descripción de «BARNACLE BLOOM» (woh_nana:603).
msgctxt "woh_nana:604"
msgid "Something rises from the tide pool. You take a step back, noticing an awful hybrid of bone, kelp, and barnacles…"
msgstr "某個東西從潮池中浮現。你退後一步，注意到這個混合了骨頭、海帶和藤壺的可怕物體……"

#. Parte de «BARNACLE BLOOM» (woh_nana:603).
msgctxt "woh_nana:605"
msgid "A parasitic tide-plant rooted in a sunken corpse."
msgstr "紮根在沉屍之中的寄生潮汐植物。"

#. Parte de «BARNACLE BLOOM» (woh_nana:603).
msgctxt "woh_nana:606"
msgid "BARNACLE BLOOM whips you with kelp-like vines!"
msgstr "藤壺花用形似海帶的藤蔓鞭打你！"

#. Parte de «BARNACLE BLOOM» (woh_nana:603).
msgctxt "woh_nana:607"
msgid "BARNACLE BLOOM shoots you with salt crystals!"
msgstr "藤壺花朝你射出了鹽結晶！"

#. Parte de «BARNACLE BLOOM» (woh_nana:603).
msgctxt "woh_nana:608"
msgid "BARNACLE BLOOM launches briny spores at you!"
msgstr "藤壺花朝你射出了鹽水孢子！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:609"
msgid "WHISPERING HIKER"
msgstr "低語登山客"

#. Descripción de «WHISPERING HIKER» (woh_nana:609).
msgctxt "woh_nana:610"
msgid "A pale figure stands ahead, swaying gently. You can see its lips moving, though no sound reaches your ears…"
msgstr "有個慘白的身影站在前方，輕柔地搖擺著。你看得見那道身影的嘴唇在開合，卻沒有任何聲音傳入耳中……"

#. Parte de «WHISPERING HIKER» (woh_nana:609).
msgctxt "woh_nana:611"
msgid "Lost in the forest, she shouted for help until the forest claimed her voice."
msgstr "她在森林裡迷路後，開始大聲呼救，直到森林最後取走了她的聲音。"

#. Parte de «WHISPERING HIKER» (woh_nana:609).
msgctxt "woh_nana:612"
msgid "A cold whisper passes through you!"
msgstr "一道冰冷的低語聲穿過了你！"

#. Parte de «WHISPERING HIKER» (woh_nana:609).
msgctxt "woh_nana:613"
msgid "Her translucent hand brushes your arm!"
msgstr "她半透明的手輕輕擦過你的手臂！"

#. Parte de «WHISPERING HIKER» (woh_nana:609).
msgctxt "woh_nana:614"
msgid "WHISPERING HIKER attacks you!"
msgstr "低語登山客攻擊你！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:615"
msgid "LIGHT SLEEPER"
msgstr "淺眠者"

#. Descripción de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:616"
msgid "<<Why does my neighbor keep banging on the pipes and screaming all night?>>"
msgstr "「為什麼鄰居要整晚敲打水管，還一直尖叫？」"

#. Opción de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615). Opciones: [begin every mystery with a TIRED status] · <<I'm not crazy!>> · <<Yet another sleepless night...>> · INBRED INHERITOR.
msgctxt "woh_nana:617"
msgid "[begin every mystery with a TIRED status]"
msgstr "[謎團開始時持有疲勞狀態]"

#. Opción de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615). Opciones: [begin every mystery with a TIRED status] · <<I'm not crazy!>> · <<Yet another sleepless night...>> · INBRED INHERITOR.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:618"
msgid "<<I'm not crazy!>>"
msgstr "「我沒有發瘋！」"

#. Opción de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615). Opciones: [begin every mystery with a TIRED status] · <<I'm not crazy!>> · <<Yet another sleepless night...>> · INBRED INHERITOR.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:619"
msgid "<<Yet another sleepless night...>>"
msgstr "「晚上又沒睡好……」"

#. Opción de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615). Opciones: [begin every mystery with a TIRED status] · <<I'm not crazy!>> · <<Yet another sleepless night...>> · INBRED INHERITOR.
msgctxt "woh_nana:620"
msgid "INBRED INHERITOR"
msgstr "近親繁衍的後繼者"

#. Parte de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
msgctxt "woh_nana:621"
msgid ""
"A gaunt figure begins crawling down the staircase on all fours, his joints bending in a way that makes you nauseous. He is clutching a bundle of children’s toys to his chest, whispering something you can’t fully understand. When he notices you watching, he smiles…\n"
"\n"
"…you’ve finally come home."
msgstr ""
"有道消瘦的身影用四肢爬下樓梯。他關節扭曲的方式令你感到作嘔。\n"
"他胸腔裡塞滿了小孩的玩具，嘴裡還唸著你無法理解的話語。\n"
"當他發現你注意到他時，他露出了笑容……\n"
"\n"
"……你終於回家了。"

#. Parte de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
msgctxt "woh_nana:622"
msgid "The last remaining heir of the mansion, twisted by generations of inbreeding and occult practices. He still lurks in the attic, searching for a new family."
msgstr "受到世代的近親繁殖與神秘學習俗而身形扭曲，豪宅最後的繼承者。他持續潛伏在閣樓，想找尋新的家人。"

#. Parte de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
msgctxt "woh_nana:623"
msgid "INBRED INHERITOR lunges at you!"
msgstr "近親繁衍的後繼者撲向了你！"

#. Parte de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
msgctxt "woh_nana:624"
msgid "INBRED INHERITOR shakes his toys violently!"
msgstr "近親繁衍的後繼者劇烈晃動他的玩具！"

#. Parte de «LIGHT SLEEPER» (woh_nana:615).
msgctxt "woh_nana:625"
msgid "INBRED INHERITOR spits blood at you!"
msgstr "近親繁衍的後繼者對你噴出了血！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:626"
msgid "MASK-MAKER"
msgstr "面具製作師"

#. Descripción de «MASK-MAKER» (woh_nana:626).
msgctxt "woh_nana:627"
msgid ""
"You spot a lantern swaying between the houses, its dull orange glow cutting through the fog.\n"
"Before you can react, a masked figure steps into view. His quiet mumbling underneath a mask seems gentle and almost friendly, but something about him freezes your blood with fear…"
msgstr ""
"有個燈籠在房屋間搖擺著，上頭灰橘色的燈光從霧中透了出來。\n"
"在你能反應過來前，有個戴面具的身影就出現在你眼底。\n"
"他面具底下的低聲呢喃聽來溫柔而友善，但他卻讓你感到恐懼，\n"
"身上血液也彷彿要凝結……"

#. Parte de «MASK-MAKER» (woh_nana:626).
msgctxt "woh_nana:628"
msgid "After the festival honoring a local mountain spirit was abandoned following a tragedy years ago, the mask-maker still wanders at night, trying to find a proper sacrifice."
msgstr "在多年前的慘劇導致祭祀當地山靈的祭典被廢棄後，這位面具製作師至今仍會在深夜遊蕩，尋找合適的祭品。"

#. Parte de «MASK-MAKER» (woh_nana:626).
msgctxt "woh_nana:629"
msgid "MASK-MAKER swings his lantern at you!"
msgstr "面具製作師用燈籠朝你揮了過來！"

#. Parte de «MASK-MAKER» (woh_nana:626).
msgctxt "woh_nana:630"
msgid "MASK-MAKER stabs you with a knife!"
msgstr "面具製作師用刀子捅你！"

#. Parte de «MASK-MAKER» (woh_nana:626).
msgctxt "woh_nana:631"
msgid "MASK-MAKER raises his withered hand!"
msgstr "面具製作師舉起他乾枯的手！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:632"
msgid "FAMILY PORTRAIT"
msgstr "全家福"

#. Descripción de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:633"
msgid ""
"A massive painting dominates the room you’ve just entered. At first glance, it’s a typical family portrait, but the longer you look, the more details seem wrong.\n"
"Their smiles are too tight, their eyes too wet. And the smallest child’s finger seems to be…\n"
"\n"
"pointing at you."
msgstr ""
"剛進到房間，你就看到眼前這幅巨大的畫。你第一眼覺得這是普通的全家福，但你看得越久，就發現越多細節不太對。\n"
"他們的笑容太僵硬、眼睛太濕，而且最小的小孩的手指，好像……\n"
"\n"
"正在指著你。"

#. Opción de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632). Opciones: look closer · tear it down.
msgctxt "woh_nana:634"
msgid "look closer"
msgstr "仔細看"

#. Opción de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632). Opciones: look closer · tear it down.
msgctxt "woh_nana:635"
msgid "tear it down"
msgstr "將畫撕下"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:636"
msgid ""
"You inspect a canvas and learn something curious. The portrait has been repainted many times, each new layer hiding a previous one.\n"
"(+10 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""
"你調查畫布時發現一件有趣的事。\n"
"這張畫像已經被人重塗了很多次，每一層都把前一張畫給蓋了過去。\n"
"（+10 經驗）"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:637"
msgid ""
"Your eyes lock with the father’s painted gaze. Your throat tightens, and for a moment, you can’t breathe.\n"
"(-2 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"你被父親畫中的凝視所吸引。\n"
"你的喉嚨緊縮，還有一陣子無法呼吸。\n"
"（-2 理智）"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:638"
msgid ""
"The massive frame snaps, and a cloud of ancient dust fills your lungs.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"巨大的相框砰一聲掉落，使得古老的塵埃灌入你的肺部。\n"
"（-1 體力）"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:639"
msgid "Contains ten new events and ten new enemy encounters."
msgstr "包含十個新事件和十個新敵人。"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:640"
msgid "You bind the enemy with the SALT-COATED ROPE!"
msgstr "你用塗鹽的繩子綁住了敵人！"

#. Parte de «FAMILY PORTRAIT» (woh_nana:632).
msgctxt "woh_nana:641"
msgid "This will only work on ghosts..."
msgstr "這只對幽靈有效……"

msgctxt "woh_nana:642"
msgid "NEW YEAR"
msgstr "新年"

msgctxt "woh_nana:643"
msgid "Finish a playthrough in the 1.2 update"
msgstr "用 1.2 的版本完成一輪遊戲"

msgctxt "woh_nana:644"
msgid "GOTTA GET RIGHT"
msgstr "恐懼來自火力不足"

msgctxt "woh_nana:645"
msgid "get three guns in one playthrough"
msgstr "在一場遊戲中獲得三把槍"

msgctxt "woh_nana:646"
msgid "FINALLY, I CAN RELAX…"
msgstr "終於能休息了……"

msgctxt "woh_nana:647"
msgid "complete the [DARK WATER] challenge"
msgstr "完成[黑水]挑戰"

msgctxt "woh_nana:648"
msgid "SAY CHEESE…"
msgstr "笑一個……"

msgctxt "woh_nana:649"
msgid "complete the [YEARBOOK] challenge"
msgstr "完成[年鑑]挑戰"

msgctxt "woh_nana:650"
msgid "…AND DIE"
msgstr "……然後去死吧"

msgctxt "woh_nana:651"
msgid "finish the photo album before entering the lighthouse"
msgstr "在進入燈塔前完成相簿"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:652"
msgid "LET’S GO HIKING"
msgstr "去爬山吧"

#. Descripción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652).
msgctxt "woh_nana:653"
msgid "investigate MOUNTAINS location ten times in one playthrough and win"
msgstr "在一輪遊戲中調查深山地點十次並獲勝"

#. Opción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652). Opciones: THE WEATHER’S... FINE? · as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough · I HATE THIS NOISE · as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION · ---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---.
msgctxt "woh_nana:654"
msgid "THE WEATHER’S... FINE?"
msgstr "天氣還……不錯？"

#. Opción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652). Opciones: THE WEATHER’S... FINE? · as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough · I HATE THIS NOISE · as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION · ---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---.
msgctxt "woh_nana:655"
msgid "as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough"
msgstr "使用登山客，並在虔誠信徒的難易度下完成遊戲"

#. Opción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652). Opciones: THE WEATHER’S... FINE? · as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough · I HATE THIS NOISE · as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION · ---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---.
msgctxt "woh_nana:656"
msgid "I HATE THIS NOISE"
msgstr "我恨噪音"

#. Opción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652). Opciones: THE WEATHER’S... FINE? · as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough · I HATE THIS NOISE · as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION · ---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---.
msgctxt "woh_nana:657"
msgid "as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION"
msgstr "使用守子裝備耳罩"

#. Opción de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652). Opciones: THE WEATHER’S... FINE? · as HIKER, complete a TRUE BELIEVER playthrough · I HATE THIS NOISE · as MORIKO, equip EAR PROTECTION · ---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---.
msgctxt "woh_nana:658"
msgid "---THE WAR FOR SHIOKAWA---"
msgstr "---鹽川爭奪戰---"

#. Parte de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652).
msgctxt "woh_nana:659"
msgid "Four rival cults have succeeded in summoning their ancient patrons, plunging our town into a nightmare of overlapping horrors..."
msgstr "四個敵對的邪教已成功召喚祂們遠古的主人。城鎮將陷入由層層恐怖交織出的惡夢……"

#. Parte de «LET’S GO HIKING» (woh_nana:652).
msgctxt "woh_nana:660"
msgid "WE ARE DOOMED: Activates the special rules of CTHAC-ATORASU, GOIZO, ATH-YOLAZSTH and ITHOTU"
msgstr "末日將至：啟用庫塔克．阿特拉斯、戈佐、亞托．尤拉斯、伊托蘇的特殊規則"

msgctxt "woh_nana:661"
msgid "WAR FOR SHIOKAWA"
msgstr "鹽川爭奪戰"

msgctxt "woh_nana:662"
msgid "HARBINGER OF FATE"
msgstr "命運預言者"

msgctxt "woh_nana:663"
msgid "complete a HARBINGER OF DOOM playthrough successfully"
msgstr "在末日預言者的難易度下破關"

msgctxt "woh_nana:664"
msgid "BEST FRIEND AWARD"
msgstr "最佳好友獎"

msgctxt "woh_nana:665"
msgid "complete the [WORLD OF FRIENDSHIP] challenge"
msgstr "完成[友誼的世界]挑戰"

msgctxt "woh_nana:666"
msgid "FEELING FRESH"
msgstr "舒適又清新"

msgctxt "woh_nana:667"
msgid "change out of your wet clothes"
msgstr "換掉你的濕衣服"

msgctxt "woh_nana:668"
msgid "EXPERT COMMUTER"
msgstr "通勤專家"

msgctxt "woh_nana:669"
msgid "take the metro ride ten times in one playthrough"
msgstr "在一輪遊戲中搭地鐵十次"

msgctxt "woh_nana:670"
msgid "SHIOKAWA HISTORY VII"
msgstr "鹽川歷史 VII"

msgctxt "woh_nana:671"
msgid "unlock 60 achievements"
msgstr "解鎖 60 項成就"

msgctxt "woh_nana:672"
msgid ""
"MISSING GIRL \n"
"2"
msgstr ""
"失蹤的女生 \n"
"2"

msgctxt "woh_nana:673"
msgid "complete the TAPES OF TERROR scenario"
msgstr "完成驚悚錄影帶的劇情"

msgctxt "woh_nana:674"
msgid "MIDNIGHT MEAT TRAIN"
msgstr "午夜人肉列車"

msgctxt "woh_nana:675"
msgid "defeat the metro stalker"
msgstr "擊敗地鐵跟蹤狂"

msgctxt "woh_nana:676"
msgid "CLOSE AND PERSONAL"
msgstr "我的魔法會撕裂你"

msgctxt "woh_nana:677"
msgid "try combat casting"
msgstr "使用咒語的戰鬥行動"

msgctxt "woh_nana:678"
msgid "PUPPET NO MORE"
msgstr "擺脫玩偶"

msgctxt "woh_nana:679"
msgid "cure MAKOTO"
msgstr "治好真琴"

msgctxt "woh_nana:680"
msgid "TRUSTY JACKET"
msgstr "可靠外套"

msgctxt "woh_nana:681"
msgid "DRY SWEATER"
msgstr "乾燥毛衣"

msgctxt "woh_nana:682"
msgid "P.E."
msgstr "P.E."

msgctxt "woh_nana:683"
msgid "MEMORY OF JUNPEI"
msgstr "純平的記憶"

msgctxt "woh_nana:684"
msgid ""
"[he... was my friend]\n"
"+1 PERCEPTION\n"
"+1 KNOWLEDGE"
msgstr ""
"[他……是我的朋友]\n"
"+1 感知\n"
"+1 知識"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:685"
msgid "MEMORY OF HITOMI"
msgstr "仁美的記憶"

#. Descripción de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:686"
msgid ""
"[she... knew me better than anyone else]\n"
"+1 damage dealt\n"
"+1 STRENGTH"
msgstr ""
"[她……比任何人都了解我]\n"
"+1 傷害\n"
"+1 力量"

#. Opción de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685). Opciones: MEMORY OF YOU · [I was... a good person] / -10% DOOM · DISTRACTED.
msgctxt "woh_nana:687"
msgid "MEMORY OF YOU"
msgstr "你的記憶"

#. Opción de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685). Opciones: MEMORY OF YOU · [I was... a good person] / -10% DOOM · DISTRACTED.
msgctxt "woh_nana:688"
msgid ""
"[I was... a good person]\n"
"-10% DOOM"
msgstr ""
"[我……是個好人]\n"
"-10% 末日"

#. Opción de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685). Opciones: MEMORY OF YOU · [I was... a good person] / -10% DOOM · DISTRACTED.
msgctxt "woh_nana:689"
msgid "DISTRACTED"
msgstr "分心"

#. Parte de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:690"
msgid ""
"As you continue your investigation, the empty slots in your photo album begin to annoy you.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe you should put the current case aside and focus on filling out the album?"
msgstr ""
"在調查的過程中，相簿中的空位開始使你心煩。\n"
"\n"
"說不定你該將目前的案件放一邊，去專心拍照？"

#. Parte de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:691"
msgid "search for enemies"
msgstr "搜尋敵人"

#. Parte de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:692"
msgid "continue with your investigation"
msgstr "繼續展開調查"

#. Parte de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:693"
msgid "You spend the next day exploring places where supposedly monsters could be seen..."
msgstr "隔天，你跑去怪物可能出現的地方搜尋了一整天……"

#. Parte de «MEMORY OF HITOMI» (woh_nana:685).
msgctxt "woh_nana:694"
msgid ""
"You decide there are more important things to worry about than a stupid album.\n"
"(-3% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"有更多事情比那個爛相簿更重要。\n"
"（-3% 末日）"

msgctxt "woh_nana:695"
msgid "MOUNTAIN PASS"
msgstr "登山口"

msgctxt "woh_nana:696"
msgid "SLOPE"
msgstr "山坡"

msgctxt "woh_nana:697"
msgid "RIDGELINE"
msgstr "山脊"

msgctxt "woh_nana:698"
msgid "ABANDONED LOOKOUT"
msgstr "廢棄瞭望台"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:699"
msgid "LESSONS"
msgstr "教訓"

#. Descripción de «LESSONS» (woh_nana:699).
msgctxt "woh_nana:700"
msgid ""
"Reaching into your backpack, your fingers touch the worn edge of an old photo. You pull it out. A younger you is standing stiffly beside your father. His hand rests heavily on your shoulder, and his smile looks practiced, not reaching his eyes.\n"
"\n"
"You absentmindedly touch your nose, feeling the spot of an old fracture. The mountains were the only place where he couldn’t follow you."
msgstr ""
"手伸進背包時，你指尖觸碰到那張老舊照片磨損的邊緣。\n"
"你將它拿了出來。照片中年幼的你僵硬地站在父親身旁。他的手沉重地壓在你的肩上，臉上的笑容也是硬擠出來的。\n"
"\n"
"你下意識地摸了摸自己的鼻子，感受著那處骨折的痕跡。深山是他唯一去不了的地方。"

#. Opción de «LESSONS» (woh_nana:699). Opciones: keep the photo · leave the photo behind.
msgctxt "woh_nana:701"
msgid "keep the photo"
msgstr "收好照片"

#. Opción de «LESSONS» (woh_nana:699). Opciones: keep the photo · leave the photo behind.
msgctxt "woh_nana:702"
msgid "leave the photo behind"
msgstr "丟下照片"

#. Parte de «LESSONS» (woh_nana:699).
msgctxt "woh_nana:703"
msgid ""
"Your father’s lessons may be the reason you’re still alive.\n"
"(+2 STAMINA / -1 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"你父親的教訓或許是你還活著的理由。\n"
"（+2 體力/-1 理智）"

#. Parte de «LESSONS» (woh_nana:699).
msgctxt "woh_nana:704"
msgid ""
"You let the wind take the old photo down the slope. You’ve learned to find your own trails.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA / +5 EXPERIENCE)"
msgstr ""
"你讓風帶走這張老照片。你已經學會開拓出自己的一條路了。\n"
"（-1 體力/+5 經驗）"

msgctxt "woh_nana:705"
msgid "BIZARRE DIAGNOSIS"
msgstr "古怪的診斷"

msgctxt "woh_nana:706"
msgid ""
"(discard): +10 EXPERIENCE\n"
"+2% DOOM"
msgstr ""
"（丟棄）：+10 經驗\n"
"+2% 末日"

msgctxt "woh_nana:707"
msgid "TOO BUSY TO HEAL"
msgstr "無暇治療"

msgctxt "woh_nana:708"
msgid ""
"(discard): -1 MAX STAMINA\n"
"get PAINKILLER"
msgstr ""
"（丟棄）：-1 體力上限\n"
"獲得止痛藥"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:709"
msgid "SHIFTING GROUND"
msgstr "移動的地表"

#. Descripción de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709).
msgctxt "woh_nana:710"
msgid ""
"You stumble as the cracks appear in the ground, as if something far below has shifted in its sleep. You can’t help but recognize the pattern of the quakes.\n"
"\n"
"Is it… breathing?"
msgstr ""
"出現在地板上的裂縫絆倒了你，這感覺就像是地底深處某個物體在睡夢中翻了身。\n"
"你忍不住發現這個震動有著規律性。\n"
"\n"
"它是在……呼吸嗎？"

#. Opción de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709). Opciones: press your ear to the ground · back away carefully.
msgctxt "woh_nana:711"
msgid "press your ear to the ground"
msgstr "將耳朵貼到地面上"

#. Opción de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709). Opciones: press your ear to the ground · back away carefully.
msgctxt "woh_nana:712"
msgid "back away carefully"
msgstr "小心地往後退"

#. Parte de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709).
msgctxt "woh_nana:713"
msgid ""
"You’ve been listening to the weird noise for far too long, but somehow, you think you understood some of the sounds.\n"
"(+SPELL / +2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"你聽著這怪異的聲響許久，但不知為何，你覺得自己聽懂了一部分的內容。\n"
"（+ 咒語/+2% 末日）"

#. Parte de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709).
msgctxt "woh_nana:714"
msgid ""
"All you’ve achieved is getting yourself covered in mud.\n"
"(+1% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"你最後只讓自己全身都沾滿泥巴。\n"
"（+1% 末日）"

#. Parte de «SHIFTING GROUND» (woh_nana:709).
msgctxt "woh_nana:715"
msgid ""
"No way you’re going to risk falling into a potential sinkhole.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"你不想承擔可能掉進天坑的風險。\n"
"（-1 體力）"

msgctxt "woh_nana:716"
msgid "XII - THE HANGED MAN"
msgstr "XII - 倒吊者"

msgctxt "woh_nana:717"
msgid "Extra damage against HUMAN enemies"
msgstr "對人類類型的敵人造成額外傷害"

msgctxt "woh_nana:718"
msgid "Gain a random ALLY"
msgstr "獲得隨機一名夥伴"

msgctxt "woh_nana:719"
msgid "The ground suddenly gives way without any warning, and SHIOKAWA slides downward into a single, bottomless sinkhole."
msgstr "地面突然無預警崩塌，鹽川就這樣向下滑落，墜入巨大的無底洞中。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:720"
msgid "Streets, buildings, and roads are erased in moments. The door of IKT-YOSIS's prison has opened."
msgstr "街道、建築物和馬路都在一瞬間被消除。通往伊克幽希牢獄的門已經開啟。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:721"
msgid "Dragged into the underground"
msgstr "被拖入地底"

msgctxt "woh_nana:722"
msgid "Rival cults spill into the streets, their hidden chants turning into open violence. Riots quickly engulf the city and the surrounding areas."
msgstr "互相對立的邪教湧入街頭，原本隱密的念咒聲也演變成公開的暴力衝突。暴動迅速吞噬了這座城鎮與周圍的地區。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:723"
msgid "No god answers the calls in the ruins of SHIOKAWA."
msgstr "在鹽川的廢墟中，沒有神明會回應那些呼喚。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:724"
msgid "Shot during riots"
msgstr "在暴動中被槍擊"

msgctxt "woh_nana:725"
msgid "The current conspiracy is fulfilled."
msgstr "目前的陰謀論已經應驗了。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:726"
msgid "TINFOIL HAT"
msgstr "錫箔帽"

msgctxt "woh_nana:727"
msgid "win a playthrough using CONSPIRACY backstory"
msgstr "在「陰謀論狂人」這個背景故事下獲勝"

msgctxt "woh_nana:728"
msgid "NIGHT OWL"
msgstr "夜貓子"

msgctxt "woh_nana:729"
msgid "win a playthrough using LIGHT SLEEPER backstory"
msgstr "在「淺眠者」這個背景故事下獲勝"

msgctxt "woh_nana:730"
msgid "METEOROPATHY"
msgstr "氣象病"

msgctxt "woh_nana:731"
msgid "Check the weather outside 5 times in a single playthrough"
msgstr "在單次遊戲期間確認外頭天氣五次"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_nana:732"
msgid "METRO STALKER"
msgstr "地鐵跟蹤狂"

#. Descripción de «METRO STALKER» (woh_nana:732).
msgctxt "woh_nana:733"
msgid ""
"The lights flicker for just a second too long as a man in a white suit slowly stands up from his seat. He doesn’t seem to be in any rush as he reaches into his suitcase and puts on a white wooden doll mask.\n"
"\n"
"You should arrive at the next station any minute now, right?…"
msgstr ""
"隨著閃爍的燈光，一名身穿白色西裝的男子也緩緩從座位上站起。他不疾不徐地伸手進手提箱，並戴上一副白色的木製玩偶面具。\n"
"\n"
"下一站應該很快就要到了吧……？"

#. Parte de «METRO STALKER» (woh_nana:732).
msgctxt "woh_nana:734"
msgid "Mr. ISOGAI truly believes that each death keeps the tunnels from collapsing."
msgstr "磯貝先生相信每條死去的生命，都是為了防止山洞坍塌。"

#. Parte de «METRO STALKER» (woh_nana:732).
msgctxt "woh_nana:735"
msgid "METRO STALKER slams his head into you!"
msgstr "地鐵跟蹤狂用頭撞向了你！"

#. Parte de «METRO STALKER» (woh_nana:732).
msgctxt "woh_nana:736"
msgid "METRO STALKER drives a knife into your side!"
msgstr "地鐵跟蹤狂用小刀刺向你身體側邊！"

#. Parte de «METRO STALKER» (woh_nana:732).
msgctxt "woh_nana:737"
msgid "METRO STALKER pushes you against a seat!"
msgstr "地鐵跟蹤狂把你推到座位上！"

msgctxt "woh_nana:738"
msgid "DOLL MASK"
msgstr "玩偶面具"

msgctxt "woh_nana:739"
msgid "+2 DAMAGE"
msgstr "+2 傷害"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:740"
msgid "<<Whoever created this mask was very talented.>>"
msgstr "「做出這個面具的人很有才華。」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:741"
msgid "wooden mask"
msgstr "木製面具"

msgctxt "woh_nana:742"
msgid "WE ARE DOOMED"
msgstr "末日將至"

msgctxt "woh_nana:743"
msgid "multiple effects"
msgstr "複數效果"

msgctxt "woh_nana:744"
msgid "AIKO"
msgstr "愛子"

msgctxt "woh_nana:745"
msgid ""
"+2 DEXTERITY\n"
"faster offensive actions"
msgstr ""
"+2 敏捷\n"
"提升攻擊行動的速度"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_nana:746"
msgid "<< Like my new haircut?>>"
msgstr "「喜歡我的新髮型嗎？」"

msgctxt "woh_nana:747"
msgid "[ATHLETE]"
msgstr "[運動員]"

msgctxt "woh_nana:748"
msgid "You've snatched a lab coat hanging on one of the chairs."
msgstr "你拿走掛在椅子上的實驗衣。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:749"
msgid "You get a nice view of the lighthouse."
msgstr "很適合在這裡望著燈塔。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:750"
msgid ""
"You spend some time setting up the telescope. You marvel over the stars and the moon until you see... it.\n"
"The blasphemous body of the god burns into your retinas."
msgstr ""
"你花了一些時間架設好望遠鏡。你驚嘆於繁星與明月之美，直到你看見了……它。\n"
"神明充滿褻瀆的身軀，深深烙印在你的視網膜上。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:751"
msgid ""
"But it doesn't end there, the image burrowing deeper and deeper...\n"
"until you fall onto the ground, dead."
msgstr ""
"但一切還沒結束。那個圖像持續往深處挖掘……\n"
"直到你倒地而死。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:752"
msgid "Brain destroyed"
msgstr "大腦遭到破壞"

msgctxt "woh_nana:753"
msgid "NOT SUMMONED YET"
msgstr "還未召喚"

msgctxt "woh_nana:754"
msgid "CALM BEFORE THE STORM"
msgstr "暴風雨前的寧靜"

msgctxt "woh_nana:755"
msgid "no effect"
msgstr "無效果"

msgctxt "woh_nana:756"
msgid "SELECT A BONUS BEFORE CONTINUING"
msgstr "選擇加成以繼續"

msgctxt "woh_nana:757"
msgid "REGAIN STAMINA"
msgstr "恢復體力"

msgctxt "woh_nana:758"
msgid "+3 STAMINA"
msgstr "+3 體力"

msgctxt "woh_nana:759"
msgid "REGAIN REASON"
msgstr "恢復理智"

msgctxt "woh_nana:760"
msgid "+3 REASON"
msgstr "+3 理智"

msgctxt "woh_nana:761"
msgid "LOWER DOOM"
msgstr "降低末日"

msgctxt "woh_nana:762"
msgid "-5% DOOM"
msgstr "-5% 末日"

msgctxt "woh_nana:763"
msgid "FINAL STAND IV"
msgstr "背水一戰 IV"

msgctxt "woh_nana:764"
msgid "reach turn 60 in ENDLESS mode"
msgstr "在無盡模式下達到 60 回合"

msgctxt "woh_nana:765"
msgid "complete 100 achievements"
msgstr "完成 100 項成就"

msgctxt "woh_nana:766"
msgid "ULTIMATE KNOWLEDGE"
msgstr "過量知識"

msgctxt "woh_nana:767"
msgid "destroy your brain"
msgstr "摧毀自身大腦"

msgctxt "woh_nana:768"
msgid "DAILY PLANNER"
msgstr "每日計畫"

msgctxt "woh_nana:769"
msgid "ACHIEVEMENTS YOU CAN GET THIS RUN"
msgstr "能在這輪遊戲中獲得的成就"

msgctxt "woh_nana:770"
msgid "Shopping for items takes precious time. (+3% DOOM)"
msgstr "購物花了你不少寶貴的時間。（+3% 末日）"

msgctxt "woh_nana:771"
msgid ""
"When you wake up, it's already night.\n"
"Trying to ask about your friend, you are met with weird reactions. As if KANA never existed...\n"
"\n"
"You rush to the operating theater yourself but are stopped by armed policemen!\n"
"\n"
"Whatever happened, the doctors must've been too late to help..."
msgstr ""
"你醒來的時候已經是晚上了。\n"
"你詢問了你朋友的狀況，卻只得到奇怪的反應，好像你朋友從未存在過……\n"
"\n"
"你想衝進手術室查看，\n"
"卻被武裝警察給擋了下來！\n"
"\n"
"不管發生了什麼，醫生一定也來不及處理了……"

msgctxt "woh_nana:772"
msgid "You manage to scrounge up some change."
msgstr "你成功找出一些零錢。"

msgctxt "woh_nana:773"
msgid "MOUNTAINS"
msgstr "深山"

msgctxt "woh_nana:774"
msgid "MOUNTAINS' THREAT LEVEL"
msgstr "深山威脅等級"

msgctxt "woh_nana:775"
msgid "TRAVEL TO MOUNTAINS"
msgstr "前往深山"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:0"
msgid "MYSTERIOUS MYTH OF MEDUSA METAMORPHOSIS"
msgstr "邪異海蜇之謎"

#. Descripción de «MYSTERIOUS MYTH OF MEDUSA METAMORPHOSIS» (woh_ni:0).
msgctxt "woh_ni:1"
msgid ""
"MYSTERIOUS MYTH OF MEDUSA METAMORPHOSIS\n"
"\n"
"Everyone is talking about this weird giant jellyfish ambushing swimmers.\n"
"\n"
"Even the local biology teacher can't identify the species as more and more people end up hurt badly."
msgstr ""
"邪異海蜇之謎\n"
"\n"
"所有人的話題都圍繞在那隻詭異的巨大水母身上。\n"
"\n"
"儘管牠不斷攻擊海邊的遊客，還造成多人重傷，但就連當地的生物老師都不清楚這個物種的來歷。"

#. Parte de «MYSTERIOUS MYTH OF MEDUSA METAMORPHOSIS» (woh_ni:0).
msgctxt "woh_ni:2"
msgid ""
"You remember, from reading an article, that a famous marine biologist is spending his vacation in the city.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe you should seek help from him?"
msgstr ""
"你記得自己在一篇文章中讀到，著名的海洋生物學家目前正在這座城市度假。\n"
"\n"
"或許你應該尋求他的協助？"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:3"
msgid "CNIDARIA STUDY"
msgstr "刺絲胞動物研究"

#. Descripción de «CNIDARIA STUDY» (woh_ni:3).
msgctxt "woh_ni:4"
msgid "Investigate the SCHOOL location twice to complete this quest."
msgstr "調查學校的地點兩次以完成此項探索。"

#. Parte de «CNIDARIA STUDY» (woh_ni:3).
msgctxt "woh_ni:5"
msgid "Some scientists say certain medusas don't age, constantly growing in size."
msgstr "幾位科學家的研究指出，某些水母不只不會變老，體型還會隨著時間不斷增大。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:6"
msgid "THE PARTLY FLOODED CAVE"
msgstr "部分淹沒的洞穴"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:7"
msgid "CLIFFSIDE CAVE"
msgstr "懸崖洞穴"

#. Descripción de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:8"
msgid ""
"The low tide reveals a semi-sunken cave. Is this the place where the BIOLOGIST is running their experiment?\n"
"\n"
"Whatever you decide to do, you should hurry. When the high tide comes, the whole cave will be submerged underwater, potentially trapping you there!"
msgstr ""
"半淹沒的洞穴在退潮時出現了。\n"
"這裡是那個生物學家做實驗的地方嗎？\n"
"\n"
"無論要做什麼，你都得抓緊時間。\n"
"等海水漲潮之後，整座洞穴就會淹沒在水底下，\n"
"你也會被困在這裡。"

#. Opción de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7). Opciones: ENTER THE CAVE · THE MEAT BEAST.
msgctxt "woh_ni:9"
msgid "ENTER THE CAVE"
msgstr "進入洞穴"

#. Opción de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7). Opciones: ENTER THE CAVE · THE MEAT BEAST.
msgctxt "woh_ni:10"
msgid "THE MEAT BEAST"
msgstr "血肉怪物"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:11"
msgid ""
"You explore the cave, trying not to slip and fall into the cold water. Hearing some weird noise from behind a corner, you brace yourself...\n"
"\n"
"A humanoid creature seems to have no skin! Its black blood courses through yellow veins, and its pale sinew and powerful muscles are visible!\n"
"\n"
"It screams and lunges at your direction!"
msgstr ""
"探索洞穴時，你走得很慢，深怕自己會滑倒並掉進水裡。這時，從角落後方傳來了詭異的聲響，讓你來得及做好心理準備……\n"
"\n"
"一個血肉外露的人形怪獸就出現在你眼前！它黑色的血液在黃色的血管內流淌，蒼白的肌腱與強健的肌肉用肉眼就能看清楚。\n"
"\n"
"這隻怪獸在嚎叫一聲後朝你撲了過來！"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:12"
msgid "ATTACK!"
msgstr "開始戰鬥！"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:13"
msgid ""
"It's only after the MEAT HORROR falls to the ground dead that you notice a bag further down the cave.\n"
"\n"
"Inside, you find a bunch of neatly folded clothes and a journal.\n"
"\n"
"It belongs to the famous marine biologist you were looking for!"
msgstr ""
"在那隻怪獸倒地後，你在洞穴的深處發現一個背包。\n"
"\n"
"裡面放了一疊整齊的衣物和一本日記。\n"
"\n"
"這背包是那個海洋生物學家的東西！"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:14"
msgid ""
"The last entry dates back to when the jellyfish attacks started.\n"
"\n"
"<<The ancient tablet I've found when exploring the caves near SHIOKAWA has... for the lack of a better word, cursed me.>>"
msgstr ""
"最後一篇日記的日期，\n"
"正好是水母開始襲擊人們的那一天。\n"
"\n"
"「我在探索鹽川附近的洞穴時發現的這塊古代石板……詛咒了我。我想不到比詛咒更貼切的說法。」"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:15"
msgid ""
"<<I can't explain this, but every other night, my skin slips off my body as if it has a mind of its own...>>\n"
"\n"
"<<It always returns to me in the morning... I just have to wait in the cave where the tablet was. What is happening to me?!>>"
msgstr ""
"「我無法清楚解釋，但每隔一個晚上，皮膚就會從我的身上自行剝落，彷彿它有了自我意識一樣……」\n"
"\n"
"「它總是會在早上回到我身上……我只要在洞穴中那塊石板的位置等待就好。這到底是怎麼一回事！？」"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:16"
msgid ""
"What will happen to the giant skin jellyfish without its host's body? You have no idea, and hopefully, you will never learn the answer yourself.\n"
"\n"
"[MYSTERIOUS MYTH OF MEDUSA METAMORPHOSIS:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"巨大的人皮水母在失去宿主後會發生什麼事？你不知道，你也希望自己永遠不會知道這個問題的答案。\n"
"\n"
"[邪異海蜇之謎：結局 A]"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:17"
msgid "[SKIN JELLYFISH]: it's still out there"
msgstr "[人皮水母]：牠仍逍遙法外"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:18"
msgid ""
"The famous biologist is spending his vacation at the seaside mansion.\n"
"\n"
"You need to take a bus there."
msgstr ""
"知名的生物學家在\n"
"海邊的豪宅度假。\n"
"\n"
"你必須搭公車前往。"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:19"
msgid ""
"Taking the bus, you can't help but notice the large number of trees that have suddenly died.\n"
"\n"
"What could be the cause?"
msgstr ""
"在公車上，你不禁注意到大量突然死去的樹木。\n"
"\n"
"這是什麼東西造成的？"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:20"
msgid "You finally arrive at the seaside. The water here is unnaturally cold and unwelco-- wait a minute..."
msgstr "你終於抵達了海邊。這裡的海水不僅又冷又——等等……"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:21"
msgid ""
"T-that's weird...\n"
"\n"
"You shouldn't be able to see the LIGHTHOUSE from this side of the bay..."
msgstr ""
"太、太詭異了……\n"
"\n"
"你記得從這一側的海灣是看不見燈塔的……"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:22"
msgid ""
"Some of the mansions are abandoned and the roads leading to them are overgrown.\n"
"\n"
"You have to, somehow, find BIOLOGIST's vacation home."
msgstr ""
"某些豪宅長年遭到廢棄，通往豪宅的路也早已雜草叢生。\n"
"\n"
"你必須設法找到生物學家度假的住處。"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:23"
msgid "You finally enter the right place. Inside, there are many jars with various jellyfish species - but where is the BIOLOGIST himself?.."
msgstr ""
"你終於進到了他度假的那棟豪宅。裡面有非常多裝有不同種水母的\n"
"罐子，但生物學家他人呢……？"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:24"
msgid ""
"Inside a dusty study, you find a map of the cliffside with one point clearly marked...\n"
"\n"
"Is this where the BIOLOGIST is performing his studies?"
msgstr ""
"你在布滿灰塵的書房中找到了一張懸崖的地圖，\n"
"上面明顯標出了一個位置……\n"
"\n"
"這是生物學家進行研究的地方嗎？"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:25"
msgid ""
"Standing on the beach, you realize something...\n"
"\n"
"The map's coastline doesn't match the actual thing... why's that?"
msgstr ""
"你站在海灘上，意識到了什麼……\n"
"\n"
"地圖上的海岸線和實際上的\n"
"並不一致……這是為什麼？"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:26"
msgid ""
"The tides! The rise and fall of sea level changes the coastline. You should wait...\n"
"\n"
"The low tide reveals a semi-sunken cave which"
msgstr ""
"是潮汐的變化！海平面的高度會改變海岸線。你必須耐心等待……\n"
"\n"
"退潮時，\n"
"半淹沒的洞穴就出現在海岸上，"

#. Parte de «CLIFFSIDE CAVE» (woh_ni:7).
msgctxt "woh_ni:27"
msgid ""
"corresponds with the point marked on the map.\n"
"\n"
"Reluctantly, you enter into the unknown..."
msgstr ""
"那也和地圖上所標出的位置相符。\n"
"\n"
"雖然你很不情願，但你還是鼓起勇氣進入了未知的洞穴……"

msgctxt "woh_ni:28"
msgid "A - SKIN JELLYFISH"
msgstr "A - 人皮水母"

msgctxt "woh_ni:29"
msgid "B - ??"
msgstr "B - ？？"

msgctxt "woh_ni:30"
msgid "C - ??"
msgstr "C - ？？"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:31"
msgid "NIGHTMARE NEWS OF THE NOISY NAILS"
msgstr "人爪魔妖殺人事件"

#. Descripción de «NIGHTMARE NEWS OF THE NOISY NAILS» (woh_ni:31).
msgctxt "woh_ni:32"
msgid ""
"NIGHTMARE NEWS OF THE NOISY NAILS\n"
"\n"
"The morbid killing spree continues as another body is found in the city's river.\n"
"\n"
"Every victim shares one common trait. Their finger and toe nails are missing...\n"
"\n"
"They've been pried off."
msgstr ""
"人爪魔妖殺人事件\n"
"\n"
"當城市的河畔中出現另一具屍體，\n"
"就表示那喪心病狂的殺人魔又得逞了。\n"
"\n"
"所有受害者都有相同的特徵。\n"
"他們手腳的指甲都不見了……\n"
"\n"
"都被拔光了。"

#. Parte de «NIGHTMARE NEWS OF THE NOISY NAILS» (woh_ni:31).
msgctxt "woh_ni:33"
msgid ""
"Why nails?\n"
"\n"
"Could the killer have a hidden motive? Are they sending a message?\n"
"You must hurry up before they claim another victim..."
msgstr ""
"為什麼要拔掉指甲？\n"
"\n"
"殺手在背後有什麼動機？他想傳達出什麼訊息？\n"
"你得趕緊行動，\n"
"以阻止他再奪走另一條人命……"

msgctxt "woh_ni:34"
msgid "MACABRE MANICURE"
msgstr "恐怖美甲"

msgctxt "woh_ni:35"
msgid "gather GOSSIP about the current mystery"
msgstr "打聽關於這個謎團的消息"

msgctxt "woh_ni:36"
msgid "Could the killing have anything to do with the father who has lost his daughter in an accident?"
msgstr "因一場意外而失去女兒的那位父親，和目前發生的連續殺人案有關嗎？"

msgctxt "woh_ni:37"
msgid "MORTUARY"
msgstr "停屍間"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:38"
msgid "KILLER ENCOUNTER"
msgstr "遭遇殺人魔"

#. Descripción de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:39"
msgid ""
"With no leads, a trip to the police station could be useful.\n"
"Your friend's cousin works there and she could help you."
msgstr ""
"由於你目前毫無線索，\n"
"你決定前往警察局。\n"
"你朋友的親戚在那裡工作，\n"
"她可以幫助你。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:40"
msgid "Time is of the essence, so you decide to take a shortcut through the abandoned building site."
msgstr ""
"時間緊迫，所以你決定抄近路，\n"
"穿越廢棄的工地。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:41"
msgid "Reluctantly, your friend's cousin gives you a photocopied file. You thank her and leave quickly."
msgstr "你朋友的親戚不情願地提供你一份影印的資料。你感謝她之後便快速離去。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:42"
msgid "The school building seems like a safe place to study the file."
msgstr "在學校大樓應該可以安心研究這些資料。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:43"
msgid "The victims of the serial killer seem to be chosen randomly. There's no obvious pattern in regard to age, sex and education."
msgstr "連環殺手似乎是隨機挑選受害者。在年齡、性別與教育方面均未出現明顯的規律。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:44"
msgid "You should continue your search in a hospital, where the victims are."
msgstr "你該繼續搜索受害者所在的醫院。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:45"
msgid "You try to sneak into the mortuary but the hospital staff is on high alert."
msgstr "你試著偷偷溜進停屍間，但醫院員工的警覺性很高。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:46"
msgid "You decide to wait here a bit. Maybe you'll manage to find a way in."
msgstr "你決定在這裡等一下。或許你會想到其他辦法進去。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:47"
msgid "One of the mortuary technicians acts strangely. He has left the building and returned twice already."
msgstr "有位停屍間的技術員很可疑。他已經離開又回來這個地方兩遍了。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:48"
msgid "Each time he comes back, an ambulance with a new victim arrives..."
msgstr ""
"每次他返回時，\n"
"一輛救護車也剛好會抵達，\n"
"載著新的受害者……"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:49"
msgid "You notice that the man keeps his hospital key in a back pocket."
msgstr "你注意到該名男子將醫院鑰匙放在背後的口袋裡。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:50"
msgid "If you could steal it, entering the hospital would be much easier."
msgstr ""
"若你能偷到鑰匙，\n"
"要進入醫院便容易得多。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:51"
msgid ""
"<<Oh, I'm sorry!>>\n"
"you excuse yourself after bumping into the man."
msgstr ""
"「啊，不好意思！」\n"
"你撞上該名男子後向他致歉。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:52"
msgid "He frowns and hurries away, not noticing that you've managed to steal his hospital keys!"
msgstr "他一臉不爽地快步離去，而沒發現你偷走了他的醫院鑰匙。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:53"
msgid "It's getting dark and the suspicious man has not returned yet."
msgstr ""
"天色越來越暗，\n"
"而可疑男子還未返回此處。"

#. Parte de «KILLER ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:38).
msgctxt "woh_ni:54"
msgid "Now is your only chance to check out the mortuary and learn about the serial killer's victims..."
msgstr "要調查連環殺手的受害者，就只能趁現在進到停屍間才行……"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:55"
msgid "ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER"
msgstr "狹路相逢"

#. Descripción de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:56"
msgid ""
"You are stopped by a tall man wearing a dirty Kabuki mask.\n"
"<<Don't make it harder than it needs to be.. Give me your fingers.>>\n"
"\n"
"You hesitate, seeing something metallic in the man's hand."
msgstr ""
"一位身材高大，\n"
"臉上戴著骯髒的歌舞伎面具的男子擋住了你。\n"
"「別想輕舉妄動……讓我看看你的手指。」\n"
"\n"
"看見男子手上握著某種金屬的物體後，\n"
"你心裡遲疑了一下。"

#. Opción de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55). Opciones: agree · try to run.
msgctxt "woh_ni:57"
msgid "agree"
msgstr "伸出手"

#. Opción de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55). Opciones: agree · try to run.
msgctxt "woh_ni:58"
msgid "try to run"
msgstr "試著逃跑"

#. Parte de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55).
msgctxt "woh_ni:59"
msgid ""
"You extend your arm and the masked man grabs your hand, studying it. Before you can protest, he takes a pair of pliers out of his pocket and rips off one of your nails.\n"
"(why? / -1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"你伸出手臂後，面具男抓住了你的手開始研究。在你有辦法抵抗前，他從口袋中掏出一把鑷子，拔下了你一片指甲。\n"
"（他瘋了嗎？/-1 體力）"

#. Parte de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55).
msgctxt "woh_ni:60"
msgid ""
"You've managed to run from the masked man.\n"
"(+5 EXP)"
msgstr ""
"你成功逃離了面具男。\n"
"（+5 經驗）"

#. Parte de «ALLEYWAY ENCOUNTER» (woh_ni:55).
msgctxt "woh_ni:61"
msgid ""
"You try to run, but trip and fall to the ground.\n"
"\n"
"The masked man jumps on you and rips off a couple of your nails with a pair of pliers.\n"
"(why? / -2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"你試著逃跑，卻整個人跌倒在地。\n"
"\n"
"面具男坐到你身上，用鑷子拔下了你幾片指甲。\n"
"（他瘋了嗎？/-2 體力）"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:62"
msgid "ALWAYS WATCHING"
msgstr "眼神"

#. Descripción de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:63"
msgid ""
"You can't shake off the feeling that you are being watched...\n"
"(-2 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"你一直覺得有人在監視你……\n"
"（-2 理智）"

#. Opción de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62). Opciones: ANOTHER VICTIM.
msgctxt "woh_ni:64"
msgid "ANOTHER VICTIM"
msgstr "下一位受害者"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:65"
msgid ""
"On your way to the next destination, you stop the tall man wearing a dirty Kabuki mask.\n"
"He is talking to a woman and slowly reaching into his pocket..."
msgstr ""
"在前往下一個目的地的路上，你看見那位身材高大，臉上戴著骯髒的歌舞伎面具的男子。\n"
"他正在與一名女子交談，手同時還緩緩伸進了口袋……"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:66"
msgid "alert the woman"
msgstr "警告女子"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:67"
msgid "run before he notices you"
msgstr "在他注意到你之前快跑"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:68"
msgid ""
"You decide to act quickly and run between the pair, screaming.\n"
"\n"
"The panicked woman flees but the masked man grabs you by your neck.\n"
"\n"
"Before you can protest, he takes a pair of pliers out of his pocket and rips off one of your nails.\n"
"(why? / -1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"你決定迅速展開行動。\n"
"你一邊大叫，一邊朝那兩人衝了過去。\n"
"\n"
"那名女子被你嚇走了，但面具男卻掐住了你的脖子。\n"
"\n"
"在你有辦法抵抗前，\n"
"他從口袋中掏出一把鑷子拔下了你一片指甲。\n"
"（他瘋了嗎？/-1 體力）"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:69"
msgid ""
"You quickly flee from the pair and pretend you can't hear the woman's screams...\n"
"(+1% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"你快速逃離現場，假裝自己聽不見女子的尖叫聲……\n"
"（+1% 末日)"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:70"
msgid "The horrible nails beast finally stops moving. Knowing you won't be able to explain it to the police, you trigger the fire alarm and escape before anyone arrives."
msgstr ""
"可怕的指甲怪物終於一動也不動。\n"
"你知道自己無法對警方解釋這一切，所以就觸發了火警，\n"
"並在任何人抵達之前逃走了。"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:71"
msgid "A father's grief led to the creation of this monster. Hopefully, they will be joined in death..."
msgstr ""
"如果那位父親沒有失去他的女兒，\n"
"那這隻怪物也不會誕生了吧。\n"
"希望他們能在死後的世界團聚……"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:72"
msgid ""
"The dreaded KABUKI KILLER finally falls to the ground, dead.\n"
"\n"
"You alert the hospital staff and soon the whole floor is swarming with police. After a brief interrogation, you're free to go."
msgstr ""
"恐怖的歌舞伎殺手終於倒在地上沒了呼吸。\n"
"\n"
"你向醫院員工說明了情況之後，\n"
"大批員警就馬上湧進了這一層樓。\n"
"你在接受警方簡短的訊問後也離開了現場。"

#. Parte de «ALWAYS WATCHING» (woh_ni:62).
msgctxt "woh_ni:73"
msgid "Two questions still remain. What did the killer do with the nails of his victims, and who broke the mortuary's window and fled before the cops arrived?"
msgstr ""
"你內心還有兩個疑問。\n"
"殺手到底用受害者的指甲做了什麼？\n"
"還有是誰打破了停屍間的窗戶，\n"
"並在所有員警抵達之前逃跑的？"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:74"
msgid "HOSPITAL CORRIDOR"
msgstr "醫院走廊"

#. Descripción de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74).
msgctxt "woh_ni:75"
msgid ""
"Using the HOSPITAL KEY, you've managed to enter the mortuary floor unnoticed.\n"
"\n"
"The hospital floor is eerily quiet. You prepare your weapon, wondering what's going to happen next."
msgstr ""
"你使用醫院鑰匙，\n"
"成功在不被注意的情況下，\n"
"進入了停屍間的樓層。\n"
"\n"
"醫院樓層安靜到有點詭異。\n"
"你準備好自己的武器，\n"
"迎接任何可能會發生的事。"

#. Opción de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74). Opciones: enter the mortuary · MORTUARY.
msgctxt "woh_ni:76"
msgid "enter the mortuary"
msgstr "進入停屍間"

#. Opción de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74). Opciones: enter the mortuary · MORTUARY.
msgctxt "woh_ni:77"
msgid "MORTUARY"
msgstr "停屍間"

#. Parte de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74).
msgctxt "woh_ni:78"
msgid ""
"The whole room has a pungent, irritating smell you can barely stand.\n"
"\n"
"All the dissection tables are empty and you're afraid to think where the bodies are now.\n"
"\n"
"You must hurry up before the suspected killer returns back."
msgstr ""
"整間房間瀰漫著令人難以忍受的刺鼻氣味。\n"
"\n"
"所有解剖桌上都是空的，而光是思考消失的屍體現在的下落就令你感到害怕。\n"
"\n"
"你必須在嫌犯返回之前盡快展開調查。"

#. Parte de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74).
msgctxt "woh_ni:79"
msgid "leave the room"
msgstr "離開房間"

#. Parte de «HOSPITAL CORRIDOR» (woh_ni:74).
msgctxt "woh_ni:80"
msgid "is that... a human nail?"
msgstr "那是……人類的指甲嗎？"

msgctxt "woh_ni:81"
msgid "A - GRIEVING FATHER"
msgstr "A - 悲痛的父親"

msgctxt "woh_ni:82"
msgid "B - UNFINISHED CHILD"
msgstr "B - 未完成的孩子"

msgctxt "woh_ni:83"
msgid "C - ??"
msgstr "C - ？？"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:84"
msgid "FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD"
msgstr "貝原村怪談"

#. Descripción de «FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD» (woh_ni:84).
msgctxt "woh_ni:85"
msgid ""
"FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD\n"
"\n"
"A group of researchers from a university in Tokyo are researching a curious rock formation. \n"
"It was discovered a few weeks ago by tourists in a village next to Shiokawa."
msgstr ""
"貝原村怪談\n"
"\n"
"東京一所大學的研究者正在研究\n"
"一塊怪異的岩石。\n"
"這塊岩石是幾週前，\n"
"由鹽川附近村子的遊客所發現。"

#. Parte de «FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD» (woh_ni:84).
msgctxt "woh_ni:86"
msgid "You've read about it in a newspaper. The sudden disappearance of the tourists was the subject of school gossip for a few days, but ultimately no one was found."
msgstr ""
"你在報紙上有看見這件事。\n"
"突然失蹤的遊客成了\n"
"學校連續好幾天的八卦主題，\n"
"但最終還是一個人都沒找到。"

#. Parte de «FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD» (woh_ni:84).
msgctxt "woh_ni:87"
msgid "The rock formation must be somehow connected to the events happening in your town. Feeling that the researchers can help you, you decide to pack yourself and visit the village yourself..."
msgstr ""
"那塊岩石一定多少與城鎮中發生的事件有關。\n"
"你覺得那些研究者可以幫上你的忙，所以決定開始打包行李，自己前往那座村子調查……"

#. Parte de «FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD» (woh_ni:84).
msgctxt "woh_ni:88"
msgid ""
"You've managed to defeat the mysterious assailant, but he flees into the woods before you can tear his mask off.\n"
"\n"
"Who was that?!"
msgstr ""
"你成功擊敗了神秘的襲擊者，但他在被你扯下面具前就逃進了森林裡。\n"
"\n"
"他是誰啊？！"

#. Parte de «FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD» (woh_ni:84).
msgctxt "woh_ni:89"
msgid ""
"MATSUDA-SAN has told you all the research notebooks are in one of the classrooms of the closed school.\n"
"\n"
"You'll have to break in."
msgstr ""
"松田先生告訴你，所有研究的筆記都放在封閉的學校裡的一間教室內。\n"
"\n"
"你得闖進去。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:90"
msgid "SCHOOL"
msgstr "學校"

msgctxt "woh_ni:91"
msgid "VILLAGE"
msgstr "村子"

msgctxt "woh_ni:92"
msgid "FOREST"
msgstr "森林"

msgctxt "woh_ni:93"
msgid "KAORI YUTO, linguist"
msgstr "語言學家由藤香織"

msgctxt "woh_ni:94"
msgid "SAKINA OKADA, geologist"
msgstr "地質學家岡田咲菜"

msgctxt "woh_ni:95"
msgid "HIROKI SHINOHE, theologist"
msgstr "神學家篠瀨宏樹"

msgctxt "woh_ni:96"
msgid ""
"The river's water level is rising and the village will soon be cut off from the outside world. Hurry up!\n"
"Researchers missing:"
msgstr ""
"河面正在升高，而村子很快就會與外界失去聯繫。動作快！\n"
"\n"
"失蹤的研究者："

msgctxt "woh_ni:97"
msgid "The river's level is too high and waves crash against the village's buildings. Run before the water devours you!"
msgstr ""
"河面太高了！\n"
"河水已經開始沖毀村子裡的房屋。\n"
"在被河水吞噬前趕快逃跑吧！"

msgctxt "woh_ni:98"
msgid "All villagers have disappeared... where are they?"
msgstr ""
"所有村民都消失了……\n"
"他們人呢？"

msgctxt "woh_ni:99"
msgid "You've managed to find one of the researchers"
msgstr "你成功找到了其中一名研究者"

msgctxt "woh_ni:100"
msgid "[goal: escape]"
msgstr "[目標：逃跑]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:101"
msgid "[goal: rescue the team or escape]"
msgstr "[目標：拯救團隊或逃跑]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:102"
msgid "[goal: search for the missing team]"
msgstr "[目標：搜索失蹤的團隊]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:103"
msgid "[goal: search the SCHOOL for notes]"
msgstr "[目標：搜索學校尋找筆記]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:104"
msgid "[goal: reach the inn]"
msgstr "[目標：抵達旅館]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:105"
msgid "You've managed to find the empty classroom MATSUDA-SAN was talking about. The researchers are gone but hopefully, the notes you've found will help you locate them."
msgstr "你成功找到松田先生說的空教室。雖然研究者不在那裡，不過希望這些筆記能幫助你找到他們。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:106"
msgid "NEGLECTED BUS STOP"
msgstr "被忽視的公車站牌"

msgctxt "woh_ni:107"
msgid "investigate the CURIOUS ROCK FORMATION"
msgstr "調查怪異的岩石"

msgctxt "woh_ni:108"
msgid "rest at the INN"
msgstr "在旅館中休息"

msgctxt "woh_ni:109"
msgid "break into the SCHOOL"
msgstr "闖入學校"

msgctxt "woh_ni:110"
msgid "check out the VILLAGE"
msgstr "查看村子"

msgctxt "woh_ni:111"
msgid "explore the FOREST"
msgstr "探索森林"

msgctxt "woh_ni:112"
msgid "KAIBARA VILLAGE - ARRIVAL\n"
msgstr "抵達貝原村\n"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_ni:113"
msgid "KAIBARA VILLAGE"
msgstr "貝原村"

#. Descripción de «KAIBARA VILLAGE» (woh_ni:113).
msgctxt "woh_ni:114"
msgid ""
"You can see the curious rock formation from the bridge leading to the village.\n"
"The researchers are nowhere to be seen.\n"
"\n"
"Did the weather scare them off?"
msgstr ""
"你可以在通往村子的橋上看見怪異的岩石。\n"
"到處都看不到研究者的身影。\n"
"\n"
"是被這裡的天氣給嚇跑了嗎？"

#. Parte de «KAIBARA VILLAGE» (woh_ni:113).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:115"
msgid ""
"<<KAIBARA VILLAGE, the final stop!>>\n"
"The bus suddenly stops as the driver opens the door.\n"
"Reluctantly, you notice you're still far from the village itself. However, before you can ask any questions, the bus's doors close..."
msgstr ""
"「終點站，貝原村到了！」\n"
"公車突然停下來之後，司機也跟著打開了車門。\n"
"你下車發現這裡離村子還有一段距離，而感到有點不滿。\n"
"但在你能說些什麼之前，公車門就關上了……"

msgctxt "woh_ni:116"
msgid "CURIOUS ROCK FORMATION"
msgstr "怪異的岩石"

msgctxt "woh_ni:117"
msgid "In the distance, you can see the village of KAIBARA."
msgstr ""
"你看見了\n"
"在遠處的貝原村。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:118"
msgid "The carved pillars are older than the village itself, and you couldn't find any information about them or the rituals they're connected with."
msgstr "有著雕刻的石柱遠比村子本身還古老，而你也查不到和石柱有關的資訊或儀式。"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:119"
msgid ""
"You enter the inn, hoping you will find the research team there.\n"
"\n"
"Every room is empty except one. In the last one, you find a visibly stressed man - MATSUDA-SAN, the expedition leader.\n"
"\n"
"<<Thank god you came. We've been attacked by the villagers and got separated. I'm worried for my colleagues!>>\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"<<The things we've learned here, the knowledge... it's too dangerous. We must escape this place as soon as possible!>>"
msgstr ""
"你進入旅館，希望能在那裡找到研究團隊。\n"
"\n"
"所有房間都空無一人，除了某間房間。你在最後的房間看見緊張的探索隊隊長——松田先生。\n"
"\n"
"「謝天謝地啊，還好你來了！我們被村民攻擊之後就被拆散了。不知道我的同事們人還好嗎……？」\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"「我們在這裡研究出的東西，那些知識……實在太過危險了。我們必須盡快逃離這個地方！」"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:120"
msgid ""
"MATSUDA-SAN gulps and looks out of the window before continuing.\n"
"\n"
"<<The last time I saw my team was at the school, we used an empty classroom to keep our research notes and equipment.\n"
"\n"
"You should look there for clues. Remember, we must flee before the river level gets too high or else... >>"
msgstr ""
"松田先生吞了吞口水，看了一下窗外後才繼續說話。\n"
"\n"
"「我最後一次看見我的團隊是在學校的時候，我們利用空教室當作據點，存放我們的筆記和裝備。\n"
"\n"
"你應該去那裡尋找線索。別忘記了，我們必須在河面過高之前逃離，否則的話……」"

msgctxt "woh_ni:121"
msgid "REST (+2 STAMINA / +2 REASON)"
msgstr "休息（+2 體力/+2 理智）"

msgctxt "woh_ni:122"
msgid "ESCAPE THE VILLAGE"
msgstr "逃離村子"

msgctxt "woh_ni:123"
msgid "LEAVE THE BUILDING"
msgstr "離開建築"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:124"
msgid "<<You shouldn't rest now.>>"
msgstr "「你現在不該休息。」"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:125"
msgid "<<You can't leave yet.>>"
msgstr "「你還不能離開。」"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:126"
msgid "<<Why are you here, you need to find the research notes!>>"
msgstr ""
"「你怎麼還在這裡？」\n"
"「你得要趕快找到那些研究筆記才行！」"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:127"
msgid ""
"MATSUDA-SAN, the expedition leader holds his suitcase in one hand and a knife in the other.\n"
"\n"
"<<This is our only chance, let's go!>>"
msgstr ""
"探索隊隊長松田先生一手提著手提箱，另一手握著刀子。\n"
"\n"
"「這是我們唯一的機會，趁現在快走！」"

msgctxt "woh_ni:128"
msgid "- blocked -"
msgstr "—無法使用—"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_ni:129"
msgid "<<You need to find at least one of my colleagues. I won't leave this place alone!>>"
msgstr ""
"「你至少要找到我的一名同事才行。\n"
"我不會拋下他們自己一個人逃走！」"

msgctxt "woh_ni:130"
msgid "You rest a bit. (+2 STAMINA / +2 REASON)"
msgstr "你休息了一會（+2 體力/+2 理智）"

msgctxt "woh_ni:131"
msgid ""
"The eldritch monster disappears as suddenly as it appeared.\n"
"\n"
"All that's left of KAIBARA village is a group of deeply confused villagers. Sadly, it's too late for MATSUDA-SAN."
msgstr ""
"駭異的怪物突然消失了，\n"
"就和它出現時一樣令人措手不及。\n"
"\n"
"整個貝原村只剩下一群神智不清的村民。\n"
"遺憾的是，你來不及拯救松田先生。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:132"
msgid ""
"The research team has parked their jeep on a hill that wasn't affected by the flood.\n"
"They drive you back to SHIOKAWA and promise that they will alert the university."
msgstr ""
"研究團隊將吉普車停在不受洪水影響的小山上。\n"
"他們將你載回鹽川，\n"
"也保證會盡快向大學通報這件事。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:133"
msgid ""
"You can only hope that help will arrive in time.\n"
"\n"
"[FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD:\n"
"ENDING B]"
msgstr ""
"你只希望救援能盡快趕到。\n"
"\n"
"[貝原村怪談：結局 B]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:134"
msgid ""
"The eldritch monster disappears as suddenly as it appeared.\n"
"\n"
"All that's left of KAIBARA village is a group of deeply confused villagers. Among them, you quickly locate the embarrassed MATSUDA-SAN."
msgstr ""
"駭異的怪物突然消失了，\n"
"就和它出現時一樣令人措手不及。\n"
"\n"
"整個貝原村只剩下一群神智不清的村民。你很快在這群村民之中發現一臉尷尬的松田先生。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:135"
msgid ""
"Luckily, the research team parked their jeep on a hill that wasn't affected by the flood.\n"
"Knowing that time is of the essence, they drive you back to SHIOKAWA and promise that they will alert the government."
msgstr ""
"幸運的是，\n"
"研究團隊將吉普車停在不受洪水影響的小山上。\n"
"他們知道現在時間緊迫，所以在將你載回鹽川之後，就向你保證會盡快向政府通報這件事。"

msgctxt "woh_ni:136"
msgid ""
"You can only hope that help will arrive in time.\n"
"\n"
"[FREAKISH FABLE OF A FRIGHTENING FLOOD:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"你只希望救援能盡快趕到。\n"
"\n"
"[貝原村怪談：結局 A]"

msgctxt "woh_ni:137"
msgid "A - TRUST THE GOVERNMENT"
msgstr "A - 相信政府"

msgctxt "woh_ni:138"
msgid "B - SABBATICAL"
msgstr "B - 學術休假"

msgctxt "woh_ni:139"
msgid "C - BIGGEST LITTLE VILLAGE"
msgstr "C - 最大的小村子"

msgctxt "woh_ni:140"
msgid "contains two new mysteries"
msgstr "包含三起全新的神秘事件"

msgctxt "woh_ni:141"
msgid "partied too hard"
