#. Parte de «FOREST OF FEAR / TAPES OF TRAGEDY» (woh_roku:210).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:228"
msgid "The TALL MAN sighs and loosens his tie. <<The cleanup is going to take longer than usual,>> he mutters as he picks up your hand and throws it into a plastic bag."
msgstr "高大的男人嘆了口氣，接著解下了領帶。「這下得花更多時間來打掃了。」他一邊低聲說道，一邊把你的手撿起來，丟進塑膠袋裡。"

msgctxt "woh_roku:229"
msgid "[FOREST OF FEAR / TAPES OF TRAGEDY: ENDING C]"
msgstr "[恐懼之森/悲劇錄影帶：結局 C]"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:230"
msgid "INSIDE THE HOUSE"
msgstr "房子裡"

#. Descripción de «INSIDE THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:230).
msgctxt "woh_roku:231"
msgid ""
"The stench of rot hits you like a wall. You begin to cough as the floorboards creak under your steps.\n"
"\n"
"You can’t help but notice as the walls shift unnaturally, as if the house itself was breathing."
msgstr ""
"腐臭味帶來的強烈衝擊，使你走在木質地板時開始咳嗽。\n"
"\n"
"你不禁注意到牆壁正在不自然地移動著，彷彿房子本身正在呼吸。"

#. Opción de «INSIDE THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:230). Opciones: INSIDE THE HOUSE (JUNPEI).
msgctxt "woh_roku:232"
msgid "INSIDE THE HOUSE (JUNPEI)"
msgstr "房子裡（純平）"

#. Parte de «INSIDE THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:230).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:233"
msgid ""
"<<It looks abandoned,>>\n"
"JUNPEI mutters while taking notes in his notebook.\n"
"\n"
"Then suddenly, the floor opens without warning."
msgstr ""
"「感覺裡面沒人住。」\n"
"純平做筆記時一邊唸唸有詞。\n"
"\n"
"突然間，他腳下的地板打開了。"

#. Parte de «INSIDE THE HOUSE» (woh_roku:230).
msgctxt "woh_roku:234"
msgid ""
"There is no scream, only a short, wet sound, then silence. You don't even manage to see him one last time. The house groans and shifts, the darkness swallows him, and the floorboards scab over. It's as though JUNPEI never existed.\n"
"\n"
"Moving on feels hopeless without him, but you have no choice."
msgstr ""
"你沒聽見尖叫聲，只聽見短促且濕潤的聲響，然後就是一陣死寂。你甚至沒機會見他最後一面。這棟房子發出陣陣呻吟並開始移動，黑暗將他徹底吞噬，地板則像結痂般重新閉合。純平彷彿從未存在過一樣。\n"
"\n"
"失去他後，前方的路顯得如此絕望，但你也只能繼續向前。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:235"
msgid "INSIDE THE HOUSE (HITOMI)"
msgstr "房子裡（仁美）"

#. Descripción de «INSIDE THE HOUSE (HITOMI)» (woh_roku:235).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:236"
msgid ""
"HITOMI gives you a reassuring smile as she moves ahead.\n"
"<<I swear, when we get back to SHIOKAWA you’re totally taking me…>>\n"
"\n"
"She doesn’t manage to finish the sentence, her speech turning to wet gurgles."
msgstr ""
"仁美走在前頭，對你露出了安心的笑容。\n"
"「等我們回到鹽川，你一定要帶我去……」\n"
"\n"
"她沒能把話說完，說話聲就化作了濕潤的咕噥聲。"

#. Parte de «INSIDE THE HOUSE (HITOMI)» (woh_roku:235).
msgctxt "woh_roku:237"
msgid ""
"A concealed blade has sprung from the wall, precise and brutal.\n"
"You gasp, seeing it buried deep in her neck.\n"
"\n"
"HITOMI tries to speak again, but only blood comes out. Her eyes search yours, wide with apology and regret."
msgstr ""
"暗藏的劍從牆壁裡彈出，精準而殘酷地刺中目標。\n"
"看見劍深深刺進她的脖子裡，使你倒抽了一口氣。\n"
"\n"
"仁美想說些什麼，卻只有血流出來。\n"
"她睜大的眼睛搜索著你的身影，眼神充滿了歉意與悔恨。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:238"
msgid "INSDDE THE HOUNSE"
msgstr "房了裡"

#. Descripción de «INSDDE THE HOUNSE» (woh_roku:238).
msgctxt "woh_roku:239"
msgid ""
"You move slower now, dragging your injured leg across warped floorboards.\n"
"\n"
"The room layout changes when you’re not looking, hallways fold inward, and the ceiling… It’s sinking lower with every step.\n"
"\n"
"The house doesn’t rush, you’re already caught."
msgstr ""
"你現在拖著受傷的腿，在變形的木地板上緩慢移動著。\n"
"\n"
"當你不注意時，房間的佈局就會開始變化。走廊向內摺疊，而你每走一步……天花板就跟著降低。\n"
"\n"
"這棟房子並不急躁，因為你早已深陷其中。"

#. Opción de «INSDDE THE HOUNSE» (woh_roku:238). Opciones: INISDD THH HOUUN.
msgctxt "woh_roku:240"
msgid "INISDD THH HOUUN"
msgstr "戶了裡"

#. Parte de «INSDDE THE HOUNSE» (woh_roku:238).
msgctxt "woh_roku:241"
msgid ""
"You think of how this was supposed to end with credits and fun memories of time spent with your best friends.\n"
"\n"
"Instead, the space slowly tightens around your chest, until breathing becomes a conscious effort."
msgstr ""
"你想起這一切本該在工作人員名單中落幕，本來應該是你與朋友之間的愉快回憶。\n"
"\n"
"然而，四周的空間卻逐漸擠壓你的胸口，使你連呼吸都變得很費力。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_roku:242"
msgid "INNNN HHH UOUUU"
msgstr "戶了ネ"

#. Descripción de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:243"
msgid ""
"When the room finally collapses, there’s no pain.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"The house cares for its new guests..."
msgstr ""
"當房間終於倒塌，疼痛已不存在。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"房子很關照新的訪客……"

#. Opción de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242). Opciones: HITOMI'S CORPSE.
msgctxt "woh_roku:244"
msgid "HITOMI'S CORPSE"
msgstr "仁美的屍體"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:245"
msgid ""
"You abruptly run into the back of JUNPEI, and wince. He stands frozen, hands clasped over his mouth. It's only when you trace his gaze upwards that you see the corpse dangling from the tree.\n"
"\n"
"JUNPEI looks away, teeth clenched..."
msgstr ""
"你突然撞上純平的背，接著眉頭皺了一下。\n"
"他整個人僵在原地，雙手緊緊摀著嘴巴。\n"
"你順著他的視線往上，看見了那具懸掛在樹上的屍體。\n"
"\n"
"純平咬緊牙關，將視線移開……"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:246"
msgid ""
"The body's eyes are burned away, charred sockets, gouges across the face, blood beneath the nails. A miserable-looking corpse.\n"
"\n"
"Despite all of that, you recognize her as HITOMI.\n"
"(+ITEM / -3 ALL)"
msgstr ""
"屍體的雙眼已被燒毀，留下焦黑的眼眶。她臉上被刻著深深的鑿痕，指甲縫中則殘留著鮮血。\n"
"眼前是具死狀悽慘的屍體。\n"
"\n"
"儘管如此，你認出她就是仁美。\n"
"（+ 物品/-3 體力/-3 理智）"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:247"
msgid ""
"<<I know, we really shouldn't have waited until the last minute. But if you think about it, doesn't the darkness really sell the atmosphere?>> JUNPEI is clearly invigorated. <<It feels like we're really diving into the legends.>>\n"
"\n"
"<<Yeah,>> you admit, unable to share his enthusiasm as the trees blot out the sky, <<that's kind of the problem.>>"
msgstr ""
"「我知道我們不該拖這麼晚，但你不覺得暗一點比較有氣氛嗎？」純平顯然興致勃勃。\n"
"「感覺我們真的在深入探索這些傳說呢。」\n"
"\n"
"「是啊，」你承認時，看著樹影逐漸遮蔽天空。這使你無法像他一樣充滿興致。\n"
"「太深入感覺也不太好呢。」"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:248"
msgid ""
"<<Trust me, this documentary will, like, TOTALLY make us famous!>>\n"
"JUNPEI can barely contain his excitement. You shoot a glance at HITOMI, who’s rolling her eyes dramatically. The girl checks the camera for the tenth time and sighs.\n"
"\n"
"<<This is dumb,>> she mutters, kicking a root. <<But I can’t let you two idiots get lost without me.>>"
msgstr ""
"「相信我，這部紀錄片絕對會讓我們紅到不行！」\n"
"純平快要無法抑制他興奮的心情。你瞄了仁美一眼，她正誇張地翻著白眼。\n"
"她檢查了相機第十次，然後嘆了口氣。\n"
"\n"
"「拍什麼鬼電影啦，」她踢著樹根低聲說道。\n"
"「但要是放你們兩個白痴去森林探險，感覺一定會迷路。」"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:249"
msgid ""
"JUNPEI keeps babbling into the camera, narrating every step. You can’t help but notice the village is eerily quiet, despite the early hour.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"You begin to question if the school project is worth it…"
msgstr ""
"純平對著相機滔滔不絕，為每個行動都加上旁白。\n"
"雖然是凌晨，但你總覺得村子異常地安靜。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"你開始後悔參加這個計畫了……"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:250"
msgid "Captured by the cult"
msgstr "被邪教徒逮到"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:251"
msgid "<<She's been walking in circles around the house for the past three hours,>> says the man dressed in a black robe, stubbing a cigarette against a tree."
msgstr "「她已經連續三個小時都在繞著這棟房子走了。」一名身穿黑色外袍，靠在樹上將煙蒂踩熄的男人說道。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:252"
msgid ""
"<<Hurry up, let's feed her to the house and get out of here.\n"
"I'm picking up my daughter from the dance class in two hours.>>"
msgstr ""
"「把她餵給房子後，就馬上離開這裡吧。」\n"
"「再兩個小時，我就要去舞蹈教室接我女兒了。」"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:253"
msgid "In the darkness, you feel acutely aware of the pressure around your neck. Your camcorder hangs there from its strap, a sharp tug with every step you take through the underbrush."
msgstr ""
"在黑暗中，你能明顯感受到脖子周圍的壓迫感。\n"
"攝影機就掛在背帶上，而你穿過灌木叢的每一步，都會感覺到它在猛力拉扯你。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:254"
msgid "The camera itself is an object of comfort, familiar, yours. But the weight of it somehow sets you on edge. As though every tug is pulling you further beyond a point of no return."
msgstr "攝影機能為你帶來安全感，是你再熟悉不過的物品，但它的重量卻莫名讓你感到不安，彷彿每次拉扯，都在將你逐漸拉往深淵。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:255"
msgid ""
"You're snapped out of your thoughts by a sharp laugh from ahead of you. Looks like HITOMI pulled another scare on JUNPEI.\n"
"\n"
"<<Oh, man, the look on your face!>> she cackles. JUNPEI groans, but gives a good-natured smile. <<I guess this is what I get for suggesting we cover the occult, isn't it?>>"
msgstr ""
"前方傳來的尖銳笑聲將你從思緒中拉回現實。\n"
"看來純平又被仁美給嚇到了。\n"
"\n"
"「你剛才的表情有夠好笑的！」她笑著說。純平發出哀怨聲，但隨即展露和藹的笑容。「身為提議要拍神秘學題材的人，受到這種報應好像也很自然。」"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:256"
msgid ""
"<<Yup,>> HITOMI replies, slapping him on the shoulder. He flinches, and she laughs again. <<It's all your fault we have to be out here for... uh, how long are we out here for?>>\n"
"\n"
"You speak up, though your voice is soft. <<We got some good B-roll from the History Club, so we don't need much, but I still wish we didn't have to come out here so late.>>"
msgstr ""
"「那當然，」仁美回應完，還重重拍了他的肩膀。\n"
"純平縮了一下，害仁美又笑了出來。「都是你啦，害我們在這裡待了……呃，我們在這裡待多久啦？」\n"
"\n"
"「我們在歷史社那邊已經拍到很多不錯的空鏡頭了，所以其實不需要拍太多，所以我是希望我們不用這麼晚跑來這裡。」你語氣微弱地說道。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de JUNPEI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:257"
msgid ""
"<<I know, we really shouldn't have waited until the last minute. But if you think about it, doesn't the darkness really sell the atmosphere?>> JUNPEI is clearly invigorated. <<It feels like we're really diving into the legends.>>\n"
"\n"
"<<Yeah,>> you admit, unable to share his enthusiasm as the trees blot out the sky, <<that's kind of the problem.>>"
msgstr ""
"「我知道我們不該拖這麼晚，但你不覺得暗一點比較有氣氛嗎？」純平顯然興致勃勃。\n"
"「感覺我們真的在深入探索這些傳說呢。」\n"
"\n"
"「是啊，」你承認時，看著樹影逐漸遮蔽天空。這使你無法像他一樣充滿興致。\n"
"「太深入感覺也不太好呢。」"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo de HITOMI.
msgctxt "woh_roku:258"
msgid ""
"<<Sorry, dude.>> HITOMI says, shrugging. <<How about we just look around, see if we find something cool, and then bail?>>\n"
"\n"
"You nod. These two have always gotten you through bad situations, even when you felt helpless. They'll protect you if there's anything out here, you tell yourself.\n"
"\n"
"You trudge on, and the forest swallows you whole."
msgstr ""
"「抱歉啦。」仁美聳了聳肩說道。「不然就到處逛逛，找點酷東西來拍，然後就閃人？」\n"
"\n"
"你點了點頭。即使是在你最無助的時候，他們也總能帶你度過難關。要是這裡真的有什麼東西，他們一定也會保護好你。\n"
"\n"
"你繼續邁開步伐，森林也將你徹底吞噬。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:259"
msgid ""
"An expression of agony overtakes the girl's face. Her hair gets tangled into the apartment's churning guts, and her flesh begins to melt apart. \n"
"\n"
"She arches her back in a voiceless scream until her pale body finally collapses in on itself."
msgstr ""
"女孩臉上的表情顯得很痛苦。她的頭髮與公寓翻騰的腸胃糾纏在一起，她的血肉也開始溶解。\n"
"\n"
"她拱起背，發出無聲的尖叫，直到她蒼白的屍體倒下為止。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:260"
msgid "When you step out of the bedroom, you find the growths of wall have become brittle. With some effort, you're finally able to force open your front door."
msgstr "當你步出臥室時，發現牆上的增生物已變得脆弱。費了一番力氣後，你終於成功推開了家門。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:261"
msgid ""
"It's a relief to be outside. You've never been so thankful to be able to walk to a convenience store.\n"
"\n"
"But you'll never sleep soundly again, now aware that you're living inside a corpse..."
msgstr ""
"能來到室外著實令你鬆了一口氣。\n"
"光是能走去便利商店，就讓你內心充滿感激。\n"
"\n"
"但你再也無法安穩入眠了，因為你現在意識到，自己住在一具屍體中……"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:262"
msgid ""
"As you strike the final blow, the girl's face twists oddly. The apartment's pulsing innards slow to a still.\n"
"\n"
"The girl mouths something you can't make out. She smiles. You blink, and she's gone. The wall is closed up and scabbed over like nothing ever happened."
msgstr ""
"在你使出致命一擊後，女孩的臉便開始嚴重扭曲變形，而公寓的內臟也漸漸沒了脈搏。\n"
"\n"
"她在張口說出一些你聽不懂的話之後，露出了一抹微笑。你接著眨了眨眼，卻發現眼前的女孩突然消失，原先開啟的牆壁也閉合了起來，彷彿剛才的事沒發生過一樣。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
msgctxt "woh_roku:263"
msgid ""
"When you dazedly stumble out of the room, things seem to have returned to normal, and your door can open again. Relieved, you take the chance to go out for a walk.\n"
"\n"
"Only a few hours later do you return to the bedroom, and find a lump beneath your bed's covers. "
msgstr ""
"在你一拐一拐地走出房間後，一切似乎都恢復正常，你的門又能再度開啟了。你鬆了一口氣，趁機出門走走。\n"
"幾小時後，你回到臥室，卻發現床罩下有顆腫塊。"

#. Parte de «INNNN HHH UOUUU» (woh_roku:242).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_roku:264"
msgid ""
"Peeling back the sheets reveals the toy that you had destroyed, the pieces held together with sections of pulsing flesh. Beside its body is a small note.\n"
"\n"
">>i'll always keep\n"
"you safe<<"
msgstr ""
"你掀開床罩，發現之前被你破壞掉的玩偶。\n"
"它的各個部分，被帶著脈搏的血肉給重新組起。\n"
"你在它身體旁邊看到一張小紙條。\n"
"\n"
"「我會\n"
"永 遠 永 遠 永 遠\n"
"在你身邊保護你的」"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_san:0"
msgid "HUNTED HEIRESS"
msgstr "逃亡中的女繼承人"

#. Descripción de «HUNTED HEIRESS» (woh_san:0).
msgctxt "woh_san:1"
msgid ""
"Name: JURI OKUSAWA\n"
"21 / FEMALE\n"
" \n"
"Something terrible is stalking JURI and with each passing day, its presence is getting nearer and nearer..."
msgstr ""
"姓名：奧澤樹里\n"
"21 歲/女性\n"
" \n"
"某個恐怖的「東西」正跟在樹里身後。\n"
"而隨著時間過去，\n"
"它的身影也越來越靠近……"

#. Parte de «HUNTED HEIRESS» (woh_san:0).
msgctxt "woh_san:2"
msgid ""
"+ PERCEPTION\n"
"- DEXTERITY\n"
"starts with FAMILY CURSE"
msgstr ""
"+ 感知\n"
"- 敏捷\n"
"遊戲開始時持有家族詛咒"

msgctxt "woh_san:3"
msgid "JURI"
msgstr "樹里"

msgctxt "woh_san:4"
msgid "RUNAWAY JACKET"
msgstr "逃亡外套"

msgctxt "woh_san:5"
msgid "ATTACK THE TEACHER"
msgstr "攻擊教師"

msgctxt "woh_san:6"
msgid "Maybe if you defeat them, the horror will end?"
msgstr "如果你擊敗了教師，這恐怖或許就會結束。"

msgctxt "woh_san:7"
msgid "You attack the teacher, dealing 7 DAMAGE."
msgstr "你攻擊了教師，造成 7 傷害。"

msgctxt "woh_san:8"
msgid "You attack the teacher, dealing 10 DAMAGE."
msgstr "你攻擊了教師，造成 10 傷害。"

msgctxt "woh_san:9"
msgid "MAGICK SWEATER"
msgstr "魔法毛衣"

msgctxt "woh_san:10"
msgid "The HORROR is slowly getting closer."
msgstr "那恐怖的「東西」正在慢慢靠近你……"

msgctxt "woh_san:11"
msgid "It's too late now."
msgstr "已經太遲了。"

msgctxt "woh_san:12"
msgid "ELUSIVE"
msgstr "捉摸不定"

msgctxt "woh_san:13"
msgid "-5% DOOM"
msgstr "-5% 末日"

msgctxt "woh_san:14"
msgid "TEST OF WILL"
msgstr "意志的考驗"

msgctxt "woh_san:15"
msgid ""
"+2 KNOWLEDGE\n"
"+2% DOOM"
msgstr ""
"+2 知識\n"
"+2% 末日"

msgctxt "woh_san:16"
msgid "ESCAPEE"
msgstr "逃亡者"

msgctxt "woh_san:17"
msgid ""
"+2 DEXTERITY\n"
"+2% DOOM"
msgstr ""
"+2 敏捷\n"
"+2% 末日"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_san:18"
msgid "ON THE RUN"
msgstr "亡命之徒"

#. Descripción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:19"
msgid "until the HORROR catches you, leveling up costs 50 EXPERIENCE less"
msgstr "在那恐怖的「東西」抓到你之前，升級所需的經驗值減少 50"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_san:20"
msgid "<<it's getting closer>>"
msgstr "「它離你不遠了」"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_san:21"
msgid "<<Here's our chance!>>"
msgstr "「機會來了！」"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_san:22"
msgid "<<Attack the enemy!>>"
msgstr "「上啊！」"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_san:23"
msgid "<<We are winning!>>"
msgstr "「就差一點了！」"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_san:24"
msgid "<<Surround the enemy!>>"
msgstr "「包圍敵人！」"

#. Opción de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18). Opciones: <<it's getting closer>> · <<Here's our chance!>> · <<Attack the enemy!>> · <<We are winning!>> · <<Surround the enemy!>> · ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK.
msgctxt "woh_san:25"
msgid "ORDER YOUR ALLIES TO ATTACK"
msgstr "指揮夥伴進行攻擊"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:26"
msgid "FLASH combat action adds a chance to dodge the incoming attack"
msgstr ""
"執行「相機閃光燈」時，\n"
"將額外提升成功閃避敵人攻擊的機率"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:27"
msgid "looking for an improvised weapon results in two items, instead of one"
msgstr "在尋找臨時武器時一次發現了兩項物品"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:28"
msgid "fell out of a window!"
msgstr "從陽台墜落摔死了！"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:29"
msgid "was hit by a truck!"
msgstr "被卡車給撞死了！"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:30"
msgid "tripped and broke their neck!"
msgstr "跌倒的時候摔斷了脖子！"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:31"
msgid "walked into an empty elevator shaft!"
msgstr "不小心掉進空蕩蕩的電梯井！"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:32"
msgid "was struck by lighting!"
msgstr "被雷給劈死了！"

#. Parte de «ON THE RUN» (woh_san:18).
msgctxt "woh_san:33"
msgid "suddenly died!"
msgstr "突然意外猝死！"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:0"
msgid "LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS"
msgstr "嗜血邪樹奇譚"

#. Descripción de «LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS» (woh_shichi:0).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:1"
msgid ""
"LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS\n"
"\n"
"Before the war, SHIOKAWA was known for its high-quality wood, praised by the most influential people in Japan.\n"
"\n"
"Over the years, logging companies have claimed more land to maximize profits, often destroying and desecrating old shrines."
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\n"
"二戰前的鹽川由於出產高品質的木材，\n"
"而深受許多日本重要人士的愛戴。\n"
"\n"
"多年下來，伐木公司為了提升利益，買下眾多土地，並拆毀和褻瀆了上頭老舊的神社。"

#. Parte de «LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS» (woh_shichi:0).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:2"
msgid ""
"One night, something weird happened.\n"
"\n"
"The logging camp disappeared, and the heavy machinery was nowhere to be seen."
msgstr ""
"這一晚，奇妙的事情發生了。\n"
"\n"
"伐木基地突然消失，重型機械設備也不見蹤影。"

#. Parte de «LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS» (woh_shichi:0).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:3"
msgid "Some say the company has found a better wood source because the cost of getting the lumber from the mountain has increased."
msgstr "有人認為是公司找到了更好的林場，畢竟在山上製造木材的成本也變高了。"

#. Parte de «LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS» (woh_shichi:0).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:4"
msgid "But that doesn’t explain why all the leaves on the trees around the camp turned crimson-red overnight. And the blood-curdling screams that could sometimes be heard at night…"
msgstr ""
"但那無法解釋為何營地附近的樹葉全在一夜間變得赤紅，\n"
"也無法解釋晚上不時傳出的駭人尖叫聲……"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:5"
msgid "OLD MONASTERY"
msgstr "老舊修道院"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:6"
msgid "TERRIBLE TIMBER"
msgstr "劣質木材"

#. Descripción de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:7"
msgid "Investigate the SEASIDE location four times to complete this quest."
msgstr "調查海邊的地點四次以完成此項探索。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:8"
msgid ""
"In one of the company’s old warehouses, you discover that they left all their equipment behind.\n"
"(+ITEM)"
msgstr ""
"你在公司的老舊倉庫裡，發現他們的所有裝備都留在那裡。\n"
"（+ 物品）"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:9"
msgid "You decide to visit the library to find any information about the logging company."
msgstr "你決定走訪圖書館，來尋找和那家伐木公司有關的任何資訊。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:10"
msgid "Maybe there’s a valid reason they left SHIOKAWA?"
msgstr "他們是有什麼原因，才離開鹽川的嗎？"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:11"
msgid "Buried in brittle newspaper clippings, you find reports of vanished workers and rituals predating the town itself."
msgstr "你在成堆的破爛新聞剪報中，找到關於工人消失和古老的儀式。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:12"
msgid "The warehouse by the docks is wide open, abandoned in eerie silence."
msgstr "碼頭旁的廢棄倉庫正門大開，傳來的只有陣陣死寂。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:13"
msgid ""
"You break into the regional office. Something has scratched deep grooves into the dusty floor.\n"
"\n"
"You can’t help but think it looks like claws, not heavy tools."
msgstr ""
"你闖進了當地的辦公室。\n"
"佈滿灰塵的地板被某種東西給抓出深深的痕跡。\n"
"\n"
"那看起來更像是爪痕，\n"
"而不是重工具鑿出來的。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:14"
msgid ""
"Among the chaos, maps show logging sites overlapping ancient shrine grounds… \n"
"\n"
"All marked with black ink."
msgstr ""
"在一片混亂中，你發現地圖上伐木場和古老神社的遺址重疊之處……\n"
"\n"
"都被用黑色墨水給做了記號。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:15"
msgid "Page after page details the company’s systematic desecration of ancient shrines, bulldozed without ceremony and replaced by logging roads."
msgstr ""
"好幾頁的報告詳述公司如何蓄意且有系統性地褻瀆古老神社。\n"
"未舉辦儀式就拆除神社後，就硬生生在上頭鋪起伐木道路。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:16"
msgid "They cut deeper into the forest than any permit allowed…"
msgstr "他們開發森林的規模，已遠遠超出規範……"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:17"
msgid "The final entry points to a forgotten monastery deep in the mountains."
msgstr "最後一項記載指向了深山中一座被遺忘的修道院。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:18"
msgid "A violent clash erupted between the monks and the logging company a day before everyone disappeared."
msgstr "在所有人消失前，僧侶和伐木公司之間曾爆發一場激烈衝突。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:19"
msgid "You take the last bus out of town. With every step into the dense forest, you can’t help but feel watched."
msgstr ""
"你搭了末班車離開城鎮。\n"
"走在濃密的森林時，你忍不住覺得有人在監視你。"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:20"
msgid "Roots twist unnaturally, and the wind carries a low moan that never seems to stop..."
msgstr "眼前盡是不自然扭曲的樹根，風帶來的低吟似乎也不曾停歇……"

#. Parte de «TERRIBLE TIMBER» (woh_shichi:6).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:21"
msgid ""
"At last, the monastery emerges from the mist. Its ancient gate stands open, beckoning you inside...\n"
"\n"
"or daring you to run."
msgstr ""
"修道院最終從霧中顯現……\n"
"\n"
"古老的大門敞開，歡迎你進入……\n"
"\n"
"也在勸你趕快逃跑。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:22"
msgid "THE MONASTERY"
msgstr "修道院"

#. Descripción de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:23"
msgid ""
"The air thickens as you cross the threshold of the monastery. Countless broken statues line the path, their mouths locked in silent screams. Inside, you can see the dried bloodstains and rusty equipment.\n"
"\n"
"Then, you feel it.\n"
"\n"
"Something vast and ancient beneath your feet, still hungry, still growing…"
msgstr ""
"當你踏入這座修道院，空氣便開始變得凝重。\n"
"道路兩旁矗立著無數殘破的石像，它們張大的嘴凝固在無聲的哀號之中。\n"
"進到裡頭，隨處可見乾涸的血跡與生鏽的設備。\n"
"\n"
"接著，你感覺到腳底下有個巨大而古老的物體，\n"
"依舊飢腸轆轆，而且持續生長著……"

#. Opción de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22). Opciones: PREPARE YOURSELF.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:24"
msgid "PREPARE YOURSELF"
msgstr "做好準備"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:25"
msgid "IT’S TOO MUCH!"
msgstr "再也受不了了！"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:26"
msgid "The bus back to SHIOKAWA sways gently. You should feel victorious, defeating a threat that would consume our city, but your hands won’t stop shaking. You press a fist to your mouth and cough; a thick, dark sap dribbles between your fingers. It’s warm and bitter."
msgstr ""
"回鹽川的公車緩緩晃動著。\n"
"得以打敗吞噬城鎮的威脅應該會讓你感到驕傲，但你的手卻止不住顫抖。\n"
"你將拳頭抵住嘴巴咳嗽，又黑又濃的樹液從你指間滴落。\n"
"那是溫的，而且嚐起來很苦。"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:27"
msgid ""
"You stare out of the window at the thinning woods, trying to convince yourself that the silence means victory. Deep down, however, you know the eldritch deity has left something behind… inside you.\n"
"\n"
"[LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"你望向窗外稀疏的樹林，\n"
"想用眼前的寧靜來說服自己其實獲得了勝利。\n"
"但在你內心深處，你知道邪駭的神靈已經將某個東西……留在你身體裡。\n"
"\n"
"[嗜血邪樹奇譚：\n"
"結局 A]"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:28"
msgid ""
"Each blow of the rusted axe echoes like a scream through the crimson forest. The trees wail as they fall, covering you in black oozing sap. Finally, the deity’s angry voice fades into a quiet guttural moan.\n"
"\n"
"Exhausted, you collapse among the stumps, knowing you’re safe now…"
msgstr ""
"生鏽斧頭的揮砍聲就像尖叫一樣，\n"
"在赤紅森林之中迴盪著。樹木倒下時發出了哀號，\n"
"黑色的濃稠樹液也將你全身蓋住。\n"
"最終，神明憤怒的聲音，\n"
"也逐漸變為來自咽喉的微弱呻吟。\n"
"\n"
"你累到倒在樹墩上，內心知道自己已經平安無事……"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:29"
msgid "You know you should feel victorious, defeating a threat that could consume our city. Instead, you just feel a weight in your chest that won’t lift. The people of SHIOKAWA may never know how close they came to being swallowed whole."
msgstr "擊敗能夠吞噬整座城鎮的威脅應該要使你感到驕傲，但你內心依舊感到沉重。鹽川人可能永遠不知道自己曾經距離被吞噬如此接近。"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:30"
msgid ""
"As the bus pulls into town, you could swear you hear the wind whisper your name, soft, patient, and far too familiar…\n"
"\n"
"[LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS:\n"
"ENDING B]"
msgstr ""
"當公車停靠在城鎮時，你覺得好像聽到風在輕聲說出了你的名字……那聲音輕柔而有耐心，聽起來還過分熟悉……\n"
"\n"
"[嗜血邪樹奇譚：\n"
"結局 B]"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:31"
msgid "The bus hums quietly as it rolls toward SHIOKAWA, but your eyes stay fixed on the passing trees. Most are green and still, but every few miles, you spot one whose leaves have turned an unnatural crimson. You fight off a panic attack, telling yourself, it’s just a trick of the light."
msgstr ""
"回程的公車一路上發著低鳴聲，但你的視線始終集中在路上的樹。\n"
"大部分的樹都又直又綠，但每隔幾公里，你就會發現有樹是呈現不自然的赤紅色。你試著穩住陣腳，告訴自己那只是光線帶來的錯覺。"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:32"
msgid ""
"As the town comes into view, a cold thought grips you:\n"
"you didn’t stop it, you just slowed it down.\n"
"\n"
"[LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS:\n"
"ENDING C]"
msgstr ""
"在城鎮映入眼簾的同時，有個殘酷的想法佔據你的腦海──\n"
"你所做的一切，都只是在暫緩悲劇發生。\n"
"[嗜血邪樹奇譚：\n"
"結局 C]"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:33"
msgid ""
"You run, lungs burning, as the monastery groans behind you. You couldn’t bear the red leaves trembling with anticipation, the groan coming from the underground.\n"
"Whatever it was, fed by the blood of the monks and the logging company, it grows stronger every day. The crimson forest will not stay confined to the mountain much longer."
msgstr ""
"你拼命奔跑，肺部感到一陣灼熱，身後的寺院正發出陣陣哀鳴。\n"
"你無法忍受那些因期待而顫動的紅葉，\n"
"以及地底深處傳來的呻吟。\n"
"無論那究竟是什麼，在吸食了僧侶與伐木工人的鮮血後，它正日益強大。\n"
"這片赤紅的森林很快就會離開這座山頭了。"

#. Parte de «THE MONASTERY» (woh_shichi:22).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:34"
msgid ""
"As you take a bus back to SHIOKAWA, the wind seems to carry one final warning.\n"
"\n"
"It has tasted blood...\n"
"and it’s still hungry.\n"
"\n"
"[LABYRINTHINE LEGEND OF THE LOATHSOME LOGGERS:\n"
"ENDING D]"
msgstr ""
"當你搭乘公車回到鹽川時，風似乎捎來了最後的警告。\n"
"\n"
"它已品嚐到鮮血的滋味……\n"
"但它仍然不滿足。\n"
"\n"
"[嗜血邪樹奇譚：\n"
"結局 D]"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:35"
msgid "CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN"
msgstr "殞星家族幽冥錄"

#. Descripción de «CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN» (woh_shichi:35).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:36"
msgid ""
"CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN\n"
"\n"
"SHIOKAWA has always attracted eccentric people. The TAKAYAMA clan was no exception.\n"
"\n"
"Obsessed with astrology, the whole family has dedicated their entire lives to futile attempts to find the secret meaning of the universe."
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\n"
"鹽川總是會吸引怪人靠近，而這句話也能套用到高山家身上。\n"
"\n"
"瘋狂迷戀占星學的這個家族，為了追尋宇宙的奧秘，將整個人生都虛耗在上頭。"

#. Parte de «CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN» (woh_shichi:35).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:37"
msgid ""
"Having built a lavish observatory on the top of the mountain, the head of the clan was sure:\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"they were closer than ever."
msgstr ""
"在山上蓋了奢侈的觀測台之後，家族領袖很確信：\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"這是他們最接近的時刻了。"

#. Parte de «CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN» (woh_shichi:35).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:38"
msgid "The whole clan supposedly disappeared one fateful night, leaving behind their earthly possessions."
msgstr "在某個命運的夜晚，所有家族成員突然消失，只留下他們在人世間的所有物。"

#. Parte de «CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN» (woh_shichi:35).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:39"
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
"The decaying mansion and the observatory still stand, but the rumors of the hikers going missing in its area worry you…"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\n"
"破敗豪宅和觀測台依然存在，但登山客在當地連番失蹤的傳聞依然使你感到擔憂……"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:40"
msgid "WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER"
msgstr "呢喃詭窟之謎"

#. Descripción de «WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER» (woh_shichi:40).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:41"
msgid ""
"WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER\n"
"\n"
"Before the researchers came, the Whispering Grotto was just a local curiosity, a cave where the twisted walls seemingly captured every sound."
msgstr ""
"呢喃詭窟之謎\n"
"\n"
"在研究者到來前，呢喃石窟只是當地人的私房景點。\n"
"據說那座洞穴裡崎嶇的牆壁能捕捉任何聲響。"

#. Parte de «WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER» (woh_shichi:40).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:42"
msgid ""
"Villagers would enter alone, whisper confessions into the dark, believing that their sins had been swallowed whole...\n"
"\n"
"But now, some of them began to spill out..."
msgstr ""
"村民會獨自前往，並對著黑暗小聲說出自白，相信這樣罪孽就能被吞噬殆盡……\n"
"\n"
"但現在，有些聲音開始洩漏出去……"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:43"
msgid "RAVENOUS RITUALS"
msgstr "貪婪的儀式"

#. Descripción de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:44"
msgid "Investigate the SCHOOL location twice to complete this QUEST."
msgstr "調查學校的地點兩次以完成此項探索。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:45"
msgid "At the hardware store, you get something to protect your ears."
msgstr "你在五金行找到能保護耳朵的東西。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:46"
msgid ""
"Your friend has gone missing while hiking in the mountains.\n"
"\n"
"You decide to help her family."
msgstr ""
"你朋友在爬山時失蹤了。\n"
"\n"
"你決定幫他的家人把他給找回來。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:47"
msgid "You begin your investigation by going to the library to check the maps and local trails."
msgstr "你前往圖書館，查找地圖和當地的路線規劃。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:48"
msgid "You find out that the area where your friend has disappeared belongs to the TAKAYAMA family."
msgstr "你發現朋友消失時的所在區域，是由高山家負責管轄。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:49"
msgid "The mentions of them are scarce, but they are described as reclusive and truly obsessed with astrology."
msgstr ""
"很少有資料提到他們。\n"
"他們曾被說是低調而瘋狂沈迷於占星學的家族。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:50"
msgid ""
"The more you learn, the weirder it becomes.\n"
"\n"
"An interview with one of the survivors…."
msgstr ""
"隨著發現越多資料，事情就越往奇怪的方向發展。\n"
"\n"
"其中一名倖存的受訪者……"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:51"
msgid "…was found starving and raving about >people made of stars< and eyes watching from the sky."
msgstr "……在被尋獲時，不僅餓得要命，嘴裡還瘋狂唸著 >由星星組成的人< 和從天上看下來的眼睛。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:52"
msgid "The trail leading to the TAKAYAMA clan's mansion is overgrown."
msgstr "通往高山家豪宅的路長滿了雜草。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:53"
msgid ""
"You can't help but feel... \n"
"watched."
msgstr ""
"你總覺得……\n"
"有什麼在看著你。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:54"
msgid "Your compass spins wildly. Are you lost?"
msgstr "指南針開始激烈旋轉。該不會迷路了？"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:55"
msgid "Hiking through the woods, you find torn clothing and strange spiral symbols carved into trees."
msgstr "走進森林後，你發現了被撕爛的衣服，以及刻在樹上的漩渦狀標記。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:56"
msgid "You finally arrive at the foot of the abandoned estate. The wrought-iron gate is twisted and rusted."
msgstr ""
"你終於抵達被遺棄的建築。\n"
"在你眼前的，是座扭曲而生鏽的熟鐵大門。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:57"
msgid "You can't help but think it was built to keep something evil inside."
msgstr ""
"你不禁猜想，這棟建築物，\n"
"肯定是為了封印住某種邪惡的存在。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:58"
msgid "Atop the cliff, the dome of the observatory creaks open like a mouth."
msgstr ""
"懸崖上，觀測台的圓頂嘎吱作響地緩緩張開，\n"
"就像是張開的嘴巴一樣。"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:59"
msgid "A strange, pulsing light glows from within, and the stars above seem to swirl unnaturally…"
msgstr ""
"從裡面透出了怪異而閃動的光線，\n"
"天空上的星星似乎也在不自然地擺動著……"

#. Parte de «RAVENOUS RITUALS» (woh_shichi:43).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:60"
msgid "Now, the grotto began to leak out the sounds. And lately, whispers have started to spill into the valley, uncovering ancient grudges and curses…"
msgstr ""
"現在石窟也開始洩漏那些聲音。\n"
"最近低語聲開始傳進山谷，使古老的惡意與詛咒重見天日……"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:61"
msgid "THE RED TREE"
msgstr "赤紅之樹"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:62"
msgid "it thirsts for more blood"
msgstr "它渴望著鮮血"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:63"
msgid ""
"You continue exploring the monastery until you find a pile of bodies of both monks and the logging company workers. Out of their bodies grows a giant tree with crimson leaves. Your vision begins to swim as you come closer.\n"
"\n"
"Just what did the bloodshed awaken?"
msgstr ""
"你持續探索著修道院，並在最後發現僧侶和伐木工人的成堆屍體。\n"
"有棵長滿赤紅樹葉的大樹長在他們屍體上。\n"
"隨著你走近這棵樹，視線也開始游移不定。\n"
"\n"
"這場血腥的紛爭到底喚起了什麼？"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:64"
msgid "GOD NAME and backstory"
msgstr "神的名字與背景故事"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:65"
msgid "GOD SKILL"
msgstr "神的技能"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:66"
msgid "You feel weaker!"
msgstr "你感到更加虛弱！"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:67"
msgid "The pollen makes it hard to breathe!"
msgstr "花粉使你感到難以呼吸。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:68"
msgid "You trip over a corpse!"
msgstr "你被屍體給絆倒了！"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:69"
msgid "CUT SMALLER TREES WITH A RUSTY AXE"
msgstr "用生鏽的斧頭砍小樹"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:70"
msgid "CUT SMALLER TREES WITH CHAINSAW"
msgstr "用電鋸砍小樹"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:71"
msgid "focus on dealing with the smaller trees growing in the room"
msgstr "專心對付長在室內的小樹"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:72"
msgid "You manage to cut down one of the smaller trees in the room…"
msgstr "你成功砍下室內的一棵小樹……"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:73"
msgid "Something under the monastery groans in pain!"
msgstr "修道院底下的某種東西發出了哀號！"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:74"
msgid "[HUNGRY TREE]: MOUNTAINS' THREAT LEVEL +1\n"
msgstr "[飢餓之樹]：深山威脅等級 +1\n"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:75"
msgid "You begin your search in the local library."
msgstr "你到當地圖書館展開調查。"

#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:76"
msgid "Buried in dusty town records are vague mentions of >>The Grotto That Listens<< and a string of vanished hikers."
msgstr ""
"你在蒙塵的城鎮紀錄中，找到有人隱約提及了\n"
"「懂得聆聽的石窟」與一連串消失的登山客。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:77"
msgid "A teacher reluctantly shares copies of student drawings from a field trip to the Grotto."
msgstr "一名老師不情願地分享了學生去石窟郊遊時畫的畫。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:78"
msgid "The entrance looks like a gaping mouth in every drawing."
msgstr "入口在每張畫裡，都像個張大的嘴。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:79"
msgid "You begin packing for a hike to the Grotto and spend the rest of the day buying necessary supplies."
msgstr "你為了爬上石窟，花了一整天在採買必需品。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:80"
msgid ""
"At the village's souvenir shop, you're warned to never speak aloud inside the cave.\n"
"It doesn't echo… it remembers."
msgstr ""
"到了村子裡的紀念品店時，有人警告你別在洞穴裡發出聲響。\n"
"洞穴不會有回聲……洞穴會記得你。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:81"
msgid "The trail to the valley is overgrown, and all birds go silent the moment you cross into the woods."
msgstr "往村子的路長滿了雜草，而在你踏進樹林裡的那一刻，鳥立刻停止鳴叫。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:82"
msgid "The wind carries words you don't understand, but your name is buried somewhere inside them."
msgstr "風聲帶著你無法聽懂的話語，但裡頭隱約參雜著你的名字。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:83"
msgid "At the base of the cliffs, you find discarded ritual masks and incense remnants rotting in the dirt."
msgstr ""
"你在懸崖底部發現被丟棄的儀式面具和殘缺的線香。\n"
"它們被扔在土裡發臭。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:84"
msgid "You finally reach the Whispering Grotto. The air around you hums softly… as if waiting for you to speak."
msgstr ""
"你終於抵達呢喃石窟。\n"
"周圍的空氣發出柔和的哼聲，彷彿在等你做出回應。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:85"
msgid "THE MOUTH OF MADNESS"
msgstr "狂亂之口"

#. Descripción de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:86"
msgid ""
"The spiraling stone walls are slick with moisture and strangely warm to the touch, like the inside of your ear. The air is thick with a thousand voices murmuring just below the edge of understanding.\n"
"Further in, you pass the remnants of the Tokyo scientists' station, battered equipment, moldy notebooks, and a crate marked with red paint. Inside lie half a dozen sticks of dynamite, forgotten but still intact."
msgstr ""
"漩渦狀的石牆光滑而潮濕，摸起來還異常溫暖，就像耳朵的內部一樣。裡面空氣沉重，來自四面八方的私語聲在講著你無法理解的話。\n"
"繼續深入後，你經過東京科學家的駐點──破舊的裝備、發霉的筆記本和用紅色油漆做了記號的箱子。\n"
"箱子裡裝著六根炸藥，被忘在這裡卻又完好無損。"

#. Opción de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85). Opciones: CONTINUE · PICK UP DYNAMITE · GO BACK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:87"
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr "繼續"

#. Opción de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85). Opciones: CONTINUE · PICK UP DYNAMITE · GO BACK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:88"
msgid "PICK UP DYNAMITE"
msgstr "撿起炸藥"

#. Opción de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85). Opciones: CONTINUE · PICK UP DYNAMITE · GO BACK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:89"
msgid "GO BACK"
msgstr "返回"

#. Parte de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:90"
msgid ""
"You reach for the dynamite. For the first time, you feel the Grotto _notice_ you.\n"
"\n"
"You tighten your grip on the stick and take another step into the dark."
msgstr ""
"你撿起了炸藥。你第一次感受到石窟注意到了你。\n"
"\n"
"你握緊手上的東西，舉步邁向了黑暗。"

#. Parte de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS» (woh_shichi:85).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:91"
msgid "You can't leave this place yet."
msgstr "你還不能離開這裡。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:92"
msgid "THE MOUTH OF MADNESS (B)"
msgstr "狂亂之口（B）"

#. Descripción de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS (B)» (woh_shichi:92).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:93"
msgid ""
"As you slowly continue your exploration of the Grotto, you finally realize what this place really was.\n"
"The cave isn't a place of forgiveness - it's a prison.\n"
"\n"
"Every whispered sin, every confession of cruelty, has been absorbed by the cave's cochlea-like chambers, echoing endlessly… growing stronger."
msgstr ""
"你在緩慢探索石窟的過程中，理解這個地方的本質。\n"
"這個洞窟不是什麼原諒之地，而是一座監獄。\n"
"\n"
"所有被低聲說出的罪孽，所有殘酷惡行的自白，都被洞穴那耳蝸狀的空間給吸收，變得更強大、成為永不停止的回聲……。"

#. Parte de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS (B)» (woh_shichi:92).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:94"
msgid "As you descend deeper, things begin to make sense. The blackened trees, silent birds, violent crimes… the curses accumulated in the Grotto have started to spill out, curling through the valley and into the ears and minds of people."
msgstr ""
"繼續往深處前進後，你也開始理解前面經歷的一切。\n"
"發黑的樹木、沉默的鳥群、暴力犯罪……都是因為沉積在石窟裡的詛咒開始外洩，在山谷間繚繞蔓延，進到人們的耳朵和內心之中。"

#. Parte de «THE MOUTH OF MADNESS (B)» (woh_shichi:92).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:95"
msgid "On the cave wall, you find a set of ancient iron chains, bolted deep into the stone. Is this how the villagers once sealed the corruption, many years before? By offering the Grotto a listener? A living vessel to keep the Grotto quiet? You keep your thoughts to yourself, and for one terrible moment, you wonder if that's the only way to make it stop."
msgstr ""
"在洞穴的牆上，你發現一組古老的鐵鍊被緊緊栓在石頭上。獻給石窟一個聆聽者？獻出有生命的容器來請石窟安靜下來？這是村民多年前阻止腐敗擴散的方法嗎？這些想法在你心中沉澱著。\n"
"你恐懼的腦海中閃過某個能阻止的方法，但你不願承認那是唯一的答案。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:96"
msgid "LOCK YOUR ALLY"
msgstr "鎖住你的夥伴"

#. Descripción de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:97"
msgid ""
"You emerge from the Grotto, the iron keys burning like sin in your hand. The whispers no longer echo through the trees, and the valley is quiet again.\n"
"\n"
"You can't bring yourself to look back. The air is lighter, and the curse is contained…"
msgstr ""
"你從石窟中逃離。充滿罪孽的鐵鑰匙灼燒你的手心。\n"
"低語聲不再迴盪於樹林間，山谷也恢復了寧靜。\n"
"\n"
"你沒有勇氣回頭看。空氣變得清新，詛咒也受到遏制……"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:98"
msgid ""
"…but the guilt will stay with you until the day you die.\n"
"\n"
"[WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER:\n"
"ENDING B]"
msgstr ""
"……但你在死之前，都將永遠帶著罪惡感而活。\n"
"\n"
"[呢喃詭窟之謎：\n"
"結局 B]"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:99"
msgid "Your friend has gone missing while hiking in the mountains. You decide to help her family."
msgstr "你的朋友在爬山時失蹤了。你決定幫他的家人把他給找回來。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:100"
msgid "You begin your investigation by going to the library to check the maps and trails."
msgstr "你前往圖書館，查找地圖和當地的路線規劃。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:101"
msgid "The area where your friend has disappeared belongs to the TAKAYAMA family."
msgstr "你發現朋友消失時的所在區域，是由高山家負責管轄。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:102"
msgid "The mentions of them are scarce, but they are described as reclusive and obsessed with the stars."
msgstr "很少有資料提到他們，但他們曾被說是低調而瘋狂沈迷於占星學的家族。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:103"
msgid "The more you learn, the weirder it becomes. An interview with one of the survivors…."
msgstr ""
"隨著發現越多資料，事情就越往奇怪的方向發展。\n"
"\n"
"其中一名倖存的受訪者……"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:104"
msgid "…was found starving and raving about >people made of stars< and eyes watching from the sky."
msgstr "……在被尋獲時，不僅餓得要命，嘴裡還瘋狂唸著 >由星星組成的人< 和從天上看下來的眼睛。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:105"
msgid "The trail to the TAKAYAMA clan's mansion is overgrown."
msgstr "通往高山家豪宅的路長滿了雜草。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:106"
msgid "You feel watched."
msgstr "好像有人在看著你。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:107"
msgid "Your compass spins wildly. Are you lost?"
msgstr "指南針開始激烈旋轉。該不會迷路了？"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:108"
msgid "Hiking through the woods, you find torn clothing and strange spiral symbols carved into trees."
msgstr "走進森林後，你發現了被撕爛的衣服，以及刻在樹上的漩渦狀標記。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:109"
msgid "You finally arrive at the foot of the abandoned estate. The wrought-iron gate is twisted and rusted."
msgstr ""
"你終於抵達被遺棄的建築。\n"
"在你眼前的，是座扭曲而生鏽的熟鐵大門。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:110"
msgid "You can't help but think it was built to keep something evil inside."
msgstr ""
"你不禁猜想，這棟建築物，\n"
"肯定是為了封印住某種邪惡的存在。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:111"
msgid "Atop the cliff, the dome of the observatory creaks open like a mouth."
msgstr ""
"懸崖上，觀測台的圓頂嘎吱作響地緩緩張開，\n"
"就像是張開的嘴巴一樣。"

#. Parte de «LOCK YOUR ALLY» (woh_shichi:96).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:112"
msgid "A strange, pulsing light glows from within, and the stars above seem to swirl unnaturally…"
msgstr ""
"從裡面透出了怪異而閃動的光線，\n"
"天空上的星星似乎也在不自然地擺動著……"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:113"
msgid "TAKAYAMA OBSERVATORY"
msgstr "高山家的觀測台"

#. Descripción de «TAKAYAMA OBSERVATORY» (woh_shichi:113).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:114"
msgid ""
"A wave of stale, frigid air drifts past you as you explore the observatory. A broken telescope leans toward the ceiling, its eyepiece cracked.\n"
"\n"
"Across the floor, chalk circles and strange symbols are drawn with unnerving precision."
msgstr ""
"探索觀測台時，一陣陳腐且冰冷的寒氣從你身邊飄過。\n"
"毀損的望遠鏡斜靠向天花板，鏡片也早已碎裂。\n"
"地板上四散著粉筆畫出的圓陣，以及精確得令人感到不安的詭異符號。"

#. Parte de «TAKAYAMA OBSERVATORY» (woh_shichi:113).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:115"
msgid ""
"The lines are… sharp, as if drawn yesterday rather than years ago. In the center of the largest circle, you spot pale figures, slowly turning their eyeless faces toward you. You recognize them from the photos.\n"
"\n"
"They are the members of the TAKAYAMA clan, trapped for decades between life and death. Their thoughts invade your mind.\n"
"\n"
">>>fIniSh wHat wE sTarTed…<<<"
msgstr ""
"那線條很……銳利，彷彿不是多年前，而是昨天才剛畫好。\n"
"你發現圓陣中央的蒼白形體，正在緩慢將無眼的臉孔轉向你。\n"
"照片裡的人就是他們。\n"
"\n"
"他們是高山家族的成員，數十年來被囚禁於生死之間。\n"
"他們的想法入侵了你的腦海。\n"
"\n"
"「幫我們完成儀式……」"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:116"
msgid "REJECT THEIR PLEAS"
msgstr "拒絕他們的請求"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:117"
msgid "PERFORM THE RITUAL"
msgstr "進行儀式"

#. Descripción de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:118"
msgid ""
"You take a step back, shaking your head. The whispers grow harsher, assaulting your mind.\n"
"Out of the corner of your eye, you notice fuel canisters leaning against the wall, no doubt used to power up the observatory. The smell of old gasoline fills your lungs, and you realize just how fragile the building is.\n"
"\n"
"A single spark could erase the clan's work forever…"
msgstr ""
"你往後退，搖了搖頭。低語聲變得更為嚴厲，開始攻擊你的思緒。\n"
"你用餘光發現靠在牆上的油桶，那肯定是用來供應觀測台的能源。老舊的汽油味灌進你的肺部，你也意識到這棟建築有多脆弱。\n"
"\n"
"一道小火花就能抹去家族的成果……"

#. Opción de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117). Opciones: FIGHT THE GHOSTS · BURN DOWN THE OBSERVATORY.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:119"
msgid "FIGHT THE GHOSTS"
msgstr "與鬼魂交戰"

#. Opción de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117). Opciones: FIGHT THE GHOSTS · BURN DOWN THE OBSERVATORY.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:120"
msgid "BURN DOWN THE OBSERVATORY"
msgstr "放火燒掉觀測台"

#. Parte de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:121"
msgid "You turn your back on the circle and grab a fuel canister, the metal freezing against your palms. The smell of gasoline fills the air as you splash it across the wooden beams."
msgstr ""
"你轉身背對圓陣並拿起了油桶。\n"
"金屬的冰冷質感傳遞到你的手掌心上。\n"
"你將汽油灑在木樑上時，刺鼻的汽油味也開始瀰漫在空氣之中。"

#. Parte de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:122"
msgid "You drop the match. The fire roars upwards, and the ghosts' whispers turn into howls of triumph. Their forms twist and break apart, scattering into the cold night air like smoke caught in the wind."
msgstr "你扔出了火柴。火勢迅速向上延燒，鬼魂的低語聲轉變為嚎叫。他們的形體開始扭曲、碎裂，在冷冽的夜晚中像是煙霧般消散。"

#. Parte de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:123"
msgid ""
"From that night on, travelers speak of pale figures wandering the mountains, their voices carried on the wind… and not all are seen from afar.\n"
"\n"
"[CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN:\n"
"ENDING D]"
msgstr ""
"從那晚起，旅行者會說起在深山中遊蕩的蒼白形體。\n"
"他們的聲音隨著微風四處迴盪……\n"
"而且，並非所有人都是從遠處看見他們。\n"
"\n"
"[殞星家族幽冥錄：\n"
"結局 D]"

#. Parte de «PERFORM THE RITUAL» (woh_shichi:117).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:124"
msgid ""
"You take a careful step forward. You quickly glance around, noting the runes and symbols. The ritual seems almost complete, and you realize you can finish it yourself. Then, a sudden thought hits you.\n"
"\n"
" Would you take its power for yourself?"
msgstr ""
"你小心地往前了一步。你迅速環繞四周，發現了符文和記號。儀式看起來就快成功，你也發現自己有能力完成它。然後，有個想法閃過你的腦海。\n"
"\n"
"要不要把這份力量挪為己用呢？"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:125"
msgid "PERFORM THE RITUAL FOR YOURSELF"
msgstr "為自己進行儀式"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:126"
msgid "PERFORM THE RITUAL FOR THEM"
msgstr "為他們進行儀式"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:127"
msgid "WHISPERING GROTTO"
msgstr "呢喃石窟"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:128"
msgid "TAKAYAMA FAMILY"
msgstr "高山家"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:129"
msgid "transcending mortality"
msgstr "超越生命的有限性"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:130"
msgid ""
"You reject the ghastly whispers begging for your help, and the observatory falls silent for a heartbeat.\n"
"\n"
"Then, the air begins to shimmer, and you find yourself surrounded by the members of the TAKAYAMA family. Their pale faces are twisted with rage.\n"
"By denying them release, you've just become their final offering to the stars…"
msgstr ""
"你拒絕了駭人低語的求助後，觀測台一瞬間安靜了下來。\n"
"\n"
"接下來，空間開始散發微光，你也發現自己被高山家族給圍繞。他們蒼白的臉龐因怒氣而扭曲。\n"
"由於你拒絕釋放他們，你便成為他們獻給星星的最後一道供品……"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:131"
msgid "BOUND SPIRITS"
msgstr "受縛的靈魂"

#. Descripción de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:132"
msgid "Their failed ritual twisted the entire bloodline into a single, bound entity. Generations of grief and obsession, all clawing for your soul."
msgstr "失敗的儀式將整個血脈扭曲為單一的實體。世代的哀愁與執念，全都準備要撕裂你的靈魂。"

#. Parte de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:133"
msgid "TAKAYAMA FAMILY chants in unison!"
msgstr "高山家族異口同聲開始念誦！"

#. Parte de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:134"
msgid "TAKAYAMA FAMILY surges forward, overwhelming you!"
msgstr "高山家族朝你湧了過來，將你整個人淹沒！"

#. Parte de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:135"
msgid "TAKAYAMA FAMILY claws at your soul!"
msgstr "高山家族準備撕裂你的靈魂！"

#. Parte de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:136"
msgid ""
"The final ghost collapses into dust, leaving the observatory silent and cold. You grab a fuel canister and pour its contents across the floorboards, before striking a match.\n"
"\n"
"The fire catches instantly, consuming the blasphemous chalk symbols and arcane runes."
msgstr ""
"最後一隻鬼魂化為灰塵，觀測台也變得又冷又安靜。你拿起油桶，將內容物倒在整個木質地板上，接著點燃了火柴。\n"
"\n"
"火勢迅速延燒，將粉筆畫成的褻瀆記號。"

#. Parte de «BOUND SPIRITS» (woh_shichi:131).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:137"
msgid ""
"By the time you arrive back at the village, the observatory is nothing but a burning silhouette against the night sky.\n"
"\n"
"The clan is gone, and the mountain is safe.\n"
"For now.\n"
"\n"
"[CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN:\n"
"ENDING C]"
msgstr ""
"當你回到村子時，觀測台已化為在夜空中燃燒的火海。\n"
"\n"
"高山家族被消滅後，山上也暫時恢復了和平。\n"
"\n"
"[殞星家族幽冥錄：\n"
"結局 C]"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:138"
msgid "[DEFEATED GHOSTS]: MOUNTAINS' THREAT LEVEL -1\n"
msgstr "[擊敗鬼魂]：深山威脅等級 -1\n"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:139"
msgid ""
"As the final words of the spell leave your lips, the air in the observatory freezes.\n"
"\n"
"Your vision suddenly fills with images of the dead stars and screaming gods."
msgstr ""
"當咒語的最後幾個字從你口中離開，觀測台裡的空氣就凝結了。\n"
"\n"
"死亡星星和神明尖叫的圖像突然充斥在你眼前。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:140"
msgid ""
"When the light fades, you stagger outside into the cold night. The clan's ruinous powers are now yours…\n"
"but so is their madness.\n"
"\n"
"[CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"當光消散，你蹣跚地走向外頭寒冷的夜晚。\n"
"家族的毀滅性力量現在都歸你……\n"
"但你也繼承了他們的瘋狂意志。\n"
"\n"
"[殞星家族幽冥錄：\n"
"結局 A]"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:141"
msgid "[TAKAYAMA POWER]: +50 EXPERIENCE, +5% DOOM\n"
msgstr "[高山之力]：+50經驗，+5% 末日\n"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:142"
msgid ""
"As the final words of the spell leave your lips, the air in the observatory freezes.\n"
"\n"
"The clan bow their heads in unison, their forms slowly unraveling into silver mist.\n"
"\n"
"A sudden warm wind sweeps through the broken dome, scattering the fog until nothing remains."
msgstr ""
"當咒語的最後幾個字從你口中離開，觀測台裡的空氣就凝結了。\n"
"\n"
"家族一齊對你鞠躬，他們的形體也逐漸瓦解成銀色的霧氣。\n"
"\n"
"一陣溫暖的風吹過破裂的圓頂，霧氣也慢慢被吹散。"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:143"
msgid ""
"You search the building for evidence of the terrible ritual and erase it all. \n"
"You decide to take a telescope as a souvenir of this otherworldly adventure…\n"
"\n"
"[CRUEL CHRONICLE OF THE CADAVEROUS CLAN:\n"
"ENDING B]"
msgstr ""
"你搜索整棟建築物，將可怕儀式的證據給全部處理掉。\n"
"你決定拿走望遠鏡，作為這趟超自然冒險的紀念品……\n"
"\n"
"[殞星家族幽冥錄：\n"
"結局 B]"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:144"
msgid "[WHAT REMAINS]: +ITEM"
msgstr "[所剩之物]：+ 物品"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:145"
msgid "[HAUNTED MOUNTAINS]: MOUNTAINS' THREAT LEVEL +1\n"
msgstr "[鬧鬼的深山]:深山威脅等級 +1\n"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:146"
msgid "A – POWER BEYOND THE STARS"
msgstr "A - 超越繁星之力"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:147"
msgid "B – REST FOR THE DAMNED"
msgstr "B - 受詛咒者的安息"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:148"
msgid "C – ASHES AND SILENCE"
msgstr "C - 灰燼與死寂"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:149"
msgid "D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS"
msgstr "D - 蔓延的亡靈"

#. Descripción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:150"
msgid ""
"You spend time learning about various rituals and curses. Hopefully, they'll be helpful.\n"
"(+3% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"你花時間學習各種儀式與詛咒。希望之後有機會派上用場。\n"
"（+3% 末日）"

#. Opción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149). Opciones: A – ROOTS OF POWER · B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER · C – AXE AND EMBERS · D – CRIMSON SPREAD · HIKING HOMEWORK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:151"
msgid "A – ROOTS OF POWER"
msgstr "A - 力量的根源"

#. Opción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149). Opciones: A – ROOTS OF POWER · B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER · C – AXE AND EMBERS · D – CRIMSON SPREAD · HIKING HOMEWORK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:152"
msgid "B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER"
msgstr "B - 森林長眠"

#. Opción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149). Opciones: A – ROOTS OF POWER · B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER · C – AXE AND EMBERS · D – CRIMSON SPREAD · HIKING HOMEWORK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:153"
msgid "C – AXE AND EMBERS"
msgstr "C - 斧頭與餘燼"

#. Opción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149). Opciones: A – ROOTS OF POWER · B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER · C – AXE AND EMBERS · D – CRIMSON SPREAD · HIKING HOMEWORK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:154"
msgid "D – CRIMSON SPREAD"
msgstr "D - 蔓延的赤紅色"

#. Opción de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149). Opciones: A – ROOTS OF POWER · B – THE FOREST'S SLUMBER · C – AXE AND EMBERS · D – CRIMSON SPREAD · HIKING HOMEWORK.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:155"
msgid "HIKING HOMEWORK"
msgstr "登山任務"

#. Parte de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:156"
msgid "Investigate the SEASIDE location twice to complete this QUEST."
msgstr "調查海邊的地點兩次以完成此項探索。"

#. Parte de «D – THE HAUNTING SPREADS» (woh_shichi:149).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:157"
msgid "The noise is getting too loud for you. The countless violent whispers, quiet curses, and eldritch incantations flood your ears. You can't go any further."
msgstr "噪音大到你無法忍受。無數暴力的低語、安靜的詛咒與邪駭的念誦聲灌注到你耳中，使你無法再向前一步。"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:158"
msgid "PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES"
msgstr "安裝炸藥"

#. Descripción de «PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES» (woh_shichi:158).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:159"
msgid "You adjust the bulky ear protection over your head, and for a moment, the Grotto falls into a blessed silence. The sound quickly returns, felt through your bones, rather than heard. Even muffled, the sounds seep in, names you've never heard, sins you've never committed, and curses passed down like blood."
msgstr "你將笨重的耳罩戴到頭上，剎那間，石窟獲得了難得的安寧。聲音很快又出現，但這次是從骨頭傳導進入。即便隔著耳罩，那些雜音仍不斷滲入。那是你聞所未聞的名字、從未犯下的罪孽，以及如血脈般代代相傳的詛咒。"

#. Parte de «PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES» (woh_shichi:158).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:160"
msgid "At the bottom of the narrowing tunnel, you find… it. An ancient stone door sealed with rusted chains and symbols etched in a language that predates humanity. You hesitate only for a moment, tearing the chains free. The whispers burst forward, flooding the space beyond like a dam collapsing. The sudden silence disorients you, and you drop your ear protection to the ground, taking a step towards the blackness."
msgstr "在狹窄的隧道盡頭，你找到了……那個東西。一扇被生鏽鐵鍊封印的古老石門，門上刻著早於人類文明的語言符號。你僅猶豫了片刻，便動手扯開了鐵鍊。剎那間，呢喃聲噴湧而出，如水壩潰堤般淹沒了門後的空間。隨之而來的死寂令你感到暈眩，你將耳罩丟到地上，朝著前方無盡的漆黑邁開了步伐。"

#. Parte de «PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES» (woh_shichi:158).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:161"
msgid "Beyond the ancient door lies a massive, lightless chamber, an impossible space. Weird shapes drift through the darkness, half-formed and pulsing with the memories of every confession ever spoken in the Grotto…"
msgstr "在那扇古老大門背後，隱藏著巨大且無光的密室──一個顯然不合常理的空間。詭異的形體在黑暗中飄盪，呈現半成形的樣貌，並隨著石窟中的每一句自白脈動著……"

#. Parte de «PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES» (woh_shichi:158).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:162"
msgid "With trembling hands, you place the dynamite sticks following the plans written by the scientists. You light the fuse and run as the cave groans like something waking up too fast."
msgstr "你照著科學家的計畫，用顫抖的手安置炸藥。你點燃導火線後隨即逃離，洞穴也呻吟得像是有什麼甦醒得太快。"

#. Parte de «PLANT THE EXPLOSIVES» (woh_shichi:158).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:163"
msgid ""
"The explosion tears through the Grotto with a deafening roar. The whispers, once sealed by the cave's walls, spill into the open air. The curses won't accumulate anymore, but with a sickening certainty, you know that the villages that lie in the valley are doomed.\n"
"\n"
"[WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER:\n"
"ENDING C]"
msgstr ""
"石窟被炸毀時，還發出震耳欲聾的咆哮聲。\n"
"過去封印在洞穴牆壁上的低語聲被放到了外界。\n"
"詛咒再也不會積累，但你已經體悟到某個令人作嘔的現實──末日即將降臨於山谷的村子。\n"
"\n"
"[呢喃詭窟之謎：\n"
"結局 C]"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:164"
msgid "A – HELL"
msgstr "A - 地獄"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:165"
msgid "B – ANOTHER VESSEL"
msgstr "B - 另一個容器"

msgctxt "woh_shichi:166"
msgid "C – FLOODED"
msgstr "C - 淹沒"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:167"
msgid "DEEP UNDERGROUND"
msgstr "地底"

#. Descripción de «DEEP UNDERGROUND» (woh_shichi:167).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:168"
msgid "You step out of the Grotto, and for a moment, there's only the rush of your heartbeat. Then, faint but unmistakable, the chirp of a bird breaks the silence. It's nothing special, just a typical call, but for you, it means everything."
msgstr "你踏出了石窟，在那瞬間，你只聽得見自己急促的心跳聲。隨後，一聲微弱卻清晰的鳥鳴打破了死寂。這僅是再平凡不過的聲音，對你而言卻意味著一切。"

#. Parte de «DEEP UNDERGROUND» (woh_shichi:167).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:169"
msgid ""
"The valley is safe again.\n"
"\n"
"[WEIRD WRITE-UP OF THE WHISPERING WONDER:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"山谷又恢復了和平。\n"
"\n"
"[呢喃詭窟之謎：\n"
"結局 A]"

#. Parte de «DEEP UNDERGROUND» (woh_shichi:167).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:170"
msgid ""
"A crushing sense of guilt washes over you—not your own, but humanity's, collective and eternal, gnawing at the roots of the world.\n"
"\n"
"You step forward, knees shaking, and wonder: did you just open the way to hell?"
msgstr ""
"沉重的罪惡感席捲而來——那並非只屬於你，而是屬於全人類、集體且永恆的罪孽，正不斷啃噬著世界的根基。\n"
"\n"
"你雙膝顫抖地向前邁出步伐，心中不禁懷疑：難道你剛才親手開啟了通往地獄的道路？"

#. Parte de «DEEP UNDERGROUND» (woh_shichi:167).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:171"
msgid ""
"CHECK OUT THE MYSTERIOUS BUILDING\n"
"[advances the clock]"
msgstr ""
"查看神秘的建築\n"
"[推進時間]"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:172"
msgid "VHS REPAIR"
msgstr "修復錄影帶"

#. Descripción de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:173"
msgid ""
"On the outskirts of the village, you find a small building nestled between farming fields. The small sign above reads 'VHS REPAIR' and the room is filled with old TVs and VCRs.\n"
"\n"
"The man sitting on a bench in front of the building is wearing a white suit. When you approach, he gives you a polite smile and puts down the teacup he was holding."
msgstr ""
"你在村子外圍的農田間發現一座小房子。上面的小牌子寫著「修復錄影帶」，房間裡也堆滿了老舊的電視和錄影帶。\n"
"\n"
"有位穿著白色套裝的男子，坐在房子前面的長椅上。當你靠近時，他給你一個禮貌的微笑，並放下他握在手上的茶杯。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:174"
msgid ""
"<<Welcome to my small shop,>> he says.\n"
"\n"
"<<I'm afraid the power went out and I won't be able to help you with anything.>>"
msgstr ""
"「歡迎來到我的小商店」他說道。\n"
"\n"
"「現在停電了，可能沒辦法幫上你的忙。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:175"
msgid ""
"The tall man stands up.\n"
"<<My oh my, Miss MAKOTO. How... unexpected.>>\n"
"He takes a step closer, and before you can react, he grabs your chin, inspecting your face.\n"
"<<Not quite right yet, I'm afraid,>> he murmurs and lets go.\n"
"\n"
"<<But... maybe you've got something for me.>>"
msgstr ""
"身材高大的男人站了起來。\n"
"「哎呀，這不是真琴小姐嗎？還真是……想不到啊。」\n"
"他往前踏了一步，並在你能反應過來之前抓住你的下巴，開始觀察你的臉。\n"
"「看來還不是時候。」他呢喃了幾聲後鬆開了手。\n"
"\n"
"「不過……說不定你有東西要給我。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:176"
msgid ""
"<<Welcome again,>> he says.\n"
"\n"
"<<I'm always happy to see old friends.>>\n"
"The man pats the bench.\n"
"\n"
"<<I'm terribly curious, do you happen to have something for me?>>"
msgstr ""
"「又見到你了。」他說道。\n"
"\n"
"「很開心能見到老朋友。」\n"
"男人拍了拍長椅。\n"
"\n"
"「我很好奇，你身上會不會剛好有東西要給我呢？」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:177"
msgid "hand over the FOREST TAPES"
msgstr "交出森林裡的錄影帶"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:178"
msgid "enjoy the tea, and leave"
msgstr "喝完茶後離開"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:179"
msgid ""
"You nod and sit next to the tall man, and you sip the offered tea in silence.\n"
"(+1 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"你點頭，接著坐到男人旁邊開始安靜地喝茶。\n"
"（+1 理智）"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:180"
msgid ""
"<<Ah yes... the tapes. Nice find, I can find a suitable buyer.>>\n"
"The tall man winks and takes the tapes from you.\n"
"\n"
"<<As for the payment...>>\n"
"(+FUNDS)"
msgstr ""
"「哦……是錄影帶啊，我能幫你找個適合的買家。」\n"
"他對你眨了眨眼，將錄影帶從你手中拿走。\n"
"\n"
"「至於給你的報酬……」\n"
"（+ 金錢）"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:181"
msgid ""
"<<Ah yes... the tapes. This will do nicely, MAKOTO. The house shall remain a secret.>>\n"
"The tall man winks and takes the tapes from you.\n"
"\n"
"<<I consider your debt to the YICTHETHATH to be paid in full.>>\n"
"He snaps a finger and you suddenly feel... whole again. Before you can say anything, someone behind you calls your name...\n"
"(-STATUS / +ALLY)"
msgstr ""
"「對……就是錄影帶。真琴，你做得很好。這棟房子不該被洩漏出去。」\n"
"高大的男人對你眨了眨眼，拿走了錄影帶。\n"
"\n"
"「我想，你欠伊克薩斯的債務已全數還清。」\n"
"他彈了聲響指，你就突然覺得……自己更完整了。\n"
"在你開口之前，有人在背後叫了你的名字……\n"
"（-狀態/+ 夥伴）"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:182"
msgid ""
"You can't help but notice how the entire school... smells.\n"
"\n"
"Almost like dead fish."
msgstr "整座學校聞起來……有種死魚的味道。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:183"
msgid "You could've sworn something moved in the walls..."
msgstr "你以為牆裡有什麼東西在動……"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:184"
msgid "You watch through your peephole as doctors in hazmat suits carry out one of your neighbors."
msgstr "你透過貓眼，看著穿著防護衣的醫生把你的鄰居給抬走。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:185"
msgid "The corridor is empty, but you feel watched."
msgstr "走廊沒有人，但你覺得有誰在監視你。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:186"
msgid ""
"Hearing footsteps in the corridor, you hide in one of the empty classrooms.\n"
"\n"
"That was close."
msgstr ""
"聽到走廊上的腳步聲，你立即躲進了空教室。\n"
"\n"
"真是驚險。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:187"
msgid "You waste your time reorganizing your clothes, again and again..."
msgstr "你把衣服一次又一次重新折好……"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:188"
msgid ""
"You notice a faint bruise on your arm.\n"
"\n"
"You don't remember getting hit."
msgstr ""
"你發現手臂上有個小瘀青。\n"
"\n"
"你不記得自己有撞到手臂。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:189"
msgid "Your knee pops as you climb the stairs. The sound reminds you of the summer you broke your leg... again."
msgstr "爬樓梯時，你的膝蓋發出喀喀聲。這聲音又使你回想起摔斷腿的那個夏天。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:190"
msgid ""
"A car passes by, its headlights sweeping across the street. In that brief flash, you see a figure wearing a familiar mask in the alley.\n"
"\n"
"When the light fades, however, they're already gone."
msgstr ""
"一輛車經過，它的車頭燈掃過了整條街。\n"
"在那短暫的亮光中，你看見小巷裡有著戴熟悉面具的身影。\n"
"\n"
"當亮光消退時，他卻早已不見蹤影。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:191"
msgid ""
"A person you pass by suddenly faints and collapses on the ground.\n"
"You don't stop to help them, even though you know it's futile..."
msgstr ""
"路過你身旁的人突然暈倒在地上。\n"
"但你也沒打算停下來協助他……"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:192"
msgid "You pause at the crosswalk to pick up a coin on the pavement. A truck speeds past, missing you by inches."
msgstr ""
"為了撿起路上的硬幣，你在斑馬線上停了下來。\n"
"一輛卡車疾駛而過，差個幾公分就會撞上你。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:193"
msgid "You can't help but notice a young woman standing perfectly still. You notice the silk glinting in her hair, on her face, in her mouth..."
msgstr ""
"你不禁注意到一名站得挺直的年輕女性。\n"
"你注意到有絲線在她頭髮上、在她臉上、在她嘴裡閃爍著……"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:194"
msgid "Thin strands of web stretch from the ceiling, glistening in the light."
msgstr "一束細長的蜘蛛網從天花板上垂下，反射著光芒。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:195"
msgid ""
"The ground trembles slightly as if something vast shifted deep below.\n"
"\n"
"Dust falls from the rooftops, unnoticed by most."
msgstr ""
"地板微微震動，彷彿地下有巨大的物體正在移動。\n"
"\n"
"灰塵從屋頂中落下，而不被多數人發現。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:196"
msgid "A low hum rises from the earth, more felt than heard..."
msgstr "一陣低沉的哼聲從地面傳來，可以直接用身體感受到……"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo de KANA.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:197"
msgid ""
"You suddenly jump when you hear a loud clap right behind your head.\n"
"<<Got you, you dumbass!>> KANA laughs but quickly frowns, seeing your tired expression.\n"
"\n"
"<<...you really need to relax sometimes,>> your friend mutters, scoffing."
msgstr ""
"從頭後方傳來的巨大拍手聲嚇得你跳了起來。\n"
"「嚇到你了吧！」可奈在看見你疲憊的眼神之後，就逐漸沒了笑容。\n"
"\n"
"「……你真的該好好放鬆一下啦。」你朋友小聲調侃著你。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:198"
msgid "KANA is whistling joyfully, seemingly unbothered by the creepy events."
msgstr "可奈愉快地吹著口哨，似乎完全沒被怪異的事件給影響心情。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:199"
msgid ""
"FUJIKO walks a step ahead, fists in her jacket pockets.\n"
"<< You've been quiet. Everything okay?>> you ask.\n"
"\n"
"She snorts, glancing back. <<Tch. Just stay alive… can't kick monsters if you're dead.>>"
msgstr ""
"不二子走在你前面，雙手握拳插在外套口袋裡。\n"
"「你都沒說話。還好吧？」你問道。\n"
"\n"
"她冷哼了一聲，回頭看向你。\n"
"「嘖，還活著啦……總不能比怪物先死吧？」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:200"
msgid "KAZUMI sighs and nervously fixes her hair."
msgstr "和美嘆了一口氣，神情不安地整理著頭髮。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo de HARU.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:201"
msgid ""
"Suddenly, you begin to cough uncontrollably. You turn around to see HARU lighting up yet another cigarette.\n"
"<<You really need to slow down with these. It's going to kill you, you know.>>\n"
"\n"
"HARU exhales right in your face, driving you into another coughing fit.\n"
"\n"
"<<I could list twenty things more likely to kill me, half of which are in your bag,>> he replies and ruffles your hair."
msgstr ""
"你突然忍不住開始咳嗽。\n"
"你轉過頭來，發現春又點了一根菸。\n"
"「你真的要少抽點啊，那東西遲早會殺了你的。」\n"
"\n"
"春直接把煙吐到你臉上，使你又開始猛烈咳嗽。\n"
"\n"
"「我能列出二十個更有可能殺死我的東西，然後你包包裡就佔了一半。」他說完，開始撥亂你的頭髮。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:202"
msgid ""
"You catch KIRIE staring at a corner of a room, her eyes unfocused. When you ask what she's looking at, she winces and flashes you an awkward grin.\n"
"<<S-sorry, I, uh, got distracted...>>"
msgstr ""
"你發現桐繪正盯著角落看，眼神顯得空洞。當你問起她正在看的東西時，她皺起眉頭，對你尷尬地笑了一下。\n"
"「對、對不起，有東西害我分心了……」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:203"
msgid ""
"KOUJI suddenly stops.\n"
"<<Wait a moment,>> he asks, raising his camera.\n"
"\n"
"<<A prize-winning shot right here.>>\n"
"You just shake your head."
msgstr ""
"浩二突然停了下來。\n"
"「等一下。」他說完舉起了相機。\n"
"\n"
"「這照片肯定會得獎。」\n"
"你聽完只是搖了搖頭。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo de MIZUKI.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:204"
msgid ""
"<<Do you think they'll write about it?>> MIZUKI asks, stepping over a pile of rubble.\n"
"\n"
"You tell her that no reporter would write a story this outlandish. MIZUKI laughs softly and adjusts her hair.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"<<Then I'll just have to make them believe it.>>"
msgstr ""
"「你覺得有人會想記錄這一切嗎？」瑞希踩過瓦礫堆時問道。\n"
"\n"
"你告訴她，沒有記者會想寫這麼離奇的故事。瑞希只是輕輕笑了一下，接著撥了撥頭髮。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"「那我只好努力讓他們相信了。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:205"
msgid ""
"YOICHI lingers a step behind, rubbing his eyes again and sighing.\n"
"<<You know what's the worst thing about this whole thing?>>\n"
"He asks with an awkward smile and doesn't wait for an answer.\n"
"\n"
"<<Paperwork afterwards.>>"
msgstr ""
"陽一在你身後停留，揉了揉眼睛後嘆了口氣。\n"
"「你知道這一切最糟糕的是什麼嗎？」\n"
"他帶著尷尬的笑容問完後，隨即自己說出了答案。\n"
"\n"
"「一切結束後的行政作業。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:206"
msgid ""
"JUNPEI adjusts his glasses, pulling out a battered notebook filled with messy sketches.\n"
"\n"
"<<Check this out — if we catch the shadows at the right angle, it'll look just like one of those cursed photos.>>\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"He grins, clearly excited, while you wonder if that's a good thing."
msgstr ""
"純平推了推眼鏡，拿出有著凌亂塗鴉的破舊筆記本。\n"
"\n"
"「你看，只要我們用正確的角度去捕捉影子，\n"
"就會看起來像是其中一張受詛咒的照片。」\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"他露齒而笑，感覺很興奮，而你在思考這麼做好不好。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:207"
msgid ""
"You notice JUNPEI mumbling under his breath as he compares strange diagrams.\n"
"<<Sorry, I just… sometimes it feels like I'm close to figuring out how this all connects.>>"
msgstr ""
"你發現純平在比對奇怪的圖表時會小聲地呢喃。\n"
"「抱歉，我只是有時候以為自己終於看清了全貌。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:208"
msgid ""
"HITOMI picks up a rock and hurls it deep into the trees, listening to it crash through the branches.\n"
"<<If there's something out there,>> she mutters, << I'd rather it come to us than keep lurking.>>"
msgstr ""
"純平撿起石頭並猛力扔進樹林深處，聽著樹枝被撞落的聲音。\n"
" 「要是外頭真的有什麼，」他低聲地說，\n"
"「我寧願牠直接現身，也不想要牠永遠潛伏在那裡。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:209"
msgid ""
"As you push through the undergrowth, HITOMI kicks a fallen branch out of the way with a smirk.\n"
"<<Heh, this forest isn't so scary. I've seen worse taking a bus after dark.>>\n"
"\n"
"Her nonchalance makes you laugh, though the silence that follows feels heavier than before."
msgstr ""
"當你撥開草叢前行時，純平露出得意的笑容，並順勢踢走了地上的樹枝。\n"
"「哈，這片森林也沒那麼可怕嘛，沒比我晚上搭公車時可怕。」\n"
"\n"
"他那漫不經心的神情讓你笑了出來，\n"
"儘管隨後的沉寂使氣氛更顯得沉重。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:210"
msgid "You spot the private investigator in a white suit in the distance. If he was hired to tail you, he’s doing a really bad job."
msgstr ""
"遠處有位穿著白色西裝的私家偵探。\n"
"如果他是被雇用來尾隨你，那他的跟蹤技巧可得再練練了。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:211"
msgid ""
"Accessing any information about the cliff-side mansions is next to impossible.\n"
"Is it just for privacy or are the any darker reasons behind it?"
msgstr ""
"非常難以獲得崖邊豪宅的任何資訊。\n"
"這單純是為了保護隱私，還是其實有什麼更黑暗的理由？"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:212"
msgid "The sea is calm today but you can’t see any fishing boats out. Strange."
msgstr "今天的海浪很平穩，但看不見任何漁船出海。真奇怪。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:213"
msgid "You can hear wailing of an ambulance siren in the distance."
msgstr "你能聽見救護車的警報聲從遠處傳來。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:214"
msgid "You spot a group of foreigners chatting quietly. Are they in SHIOKAWA just for the museum opening?"
msgstr "有群異地來的人在安靜地聊天。他們來鹽川是在等博物館開幕嗎？"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:215"
msgid ""
"You catch IWA seasoning something in a dented pan mid-hallway.\n"
"<<Where did you even get that?>>\n"
"\n"
"He snorts.\n"
"<<A chef never reveals his sources. Eat up. Builds muscle.>>"
msgstr ""
"岩站在走廊上，用凹陷的平底鍋煮著某種東西。\n"
"「那東西是打哪來的？」\n"
"\n"
"他哼了一聲。\n"
"「沒有廚師會透露他的食材來源。吃光它才會長肌肉。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:216"
msgid ""
"IWA pats you in the back, making you stumble.\n"
"\n"
"<<You need to hit the gym, little friend.>>\n"
"He flexes his muscles and grins.\n"
"<<I’m the best.>>"
msgstr ""
"岩拍了你的背，使你跌坐在地。\n"
"\n"
"「小毛頭，去多練點肌肉吧。」\n"
"他開始秀肌肉，並露出一抹微笑。\n"
"「我最棒。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo de ASATO.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:217"
msgid ""
"You struggle to pronounce a strange phrase.\n"
"<<No, softer,>> ASATO corrects gently.\n"
"\n"
"The air shifts as you try again.\n"
"\n"
"<<Good. One day you won’t need me to cast it for you.>>"
msgstr ""
"你試圖唸出某個奇怪的語句。\n"
"「唸輕一點」，淺藤輕聲糾正你。\n"
"\n"
"重新唸一遍後，周圍空氣也開始飄移。\n"
"\n"
"「很好。很快你就不用我來幫你施咒了。」"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:218"
msgid ""
"You pause as the dog stops to sniff a bush.\n"
"\n"
"Silly dog."
msgstr ""
"小狗停下來開始聞樹叢，你也跟著停下腳步。\n"
"\n"
"真是條傻狗狗。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:219"
msgid "The dog’s tail wags like he knows something you don’t."
msgstr "狗尾巴搖得很大力，彷彿他知道些什麼秘密。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_shichi:220"
msgid ""
"You find HERMIT staring at a wall covered in frantic chalk symbols.\n"
"\n"
"<<w-we can g-go now,>> they say quietly after a while."
msgstr ""
"隱士盯著牆壁滿滿用粉筆畫的瘋狂記號。\n"
"\n"
"過了一陣子，他安靜地說道：「該、該走了」。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:221"
msgid ""
"(LMB): select mystery\n"
"(RMB): lock mystery"
msgstr ""
"（滑鼠左鍵）：選擇謎團\n"
"（滑鼠右鍵）：鎖定謎團"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:222"
msgid "RYOKO takes the lead, pushing forward and you barely keep up."
msgstr "涼子走在最前頭，你感覺快跟不上她了。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:223"
msgid "Your sock grows damp with blood."
msgstr "襪子全被血給浸濕了。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:224"
msgid "For a few minutes, it begins to snow. Then it's over, like a dream."
msgstr "幾分鐘後，天空開始下起了雪。接著，雪停了，就像是做了一場夢。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:225"
msgid "You keep going because there is nothing else you can do."
msgstr "你繼續向前，因為這是你唯一能做的事。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:226"
msgid "Each time you stop to catch your breath, getting up again seems more unlikely."
msgstr "你每次停下來調整呼吸，就感覺越難重新振作起來。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:227"
msgid "There could be another trap under any of these bushes."
msgstr "樹叢下可能會有另一個陷阱。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:228"
msgid "The fog is so thick you can barely breathe."
msgstr "霧濃到你難以呼吸。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:229"
msgid "The same trees, again, and again, and again, and again..."
msgstr "同樣的樹一遍又一遍，一遍又一遍映入你的眼簾。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:230"
msgid "The forest won't let you go anymore."
msgstr "森林已經不打算放你走了。"

#. Parte de «VHS REPAIR» (woh_shichi:172).
msgctxt "woh_shichi:231"
msgid "Are you being followed?"
msgstr "你被跟蹤了嗎？"

