#. Notas de una versión del juego.
msgctxt "woh_ver:0"
msgid ""
"1.2 AS BELOW SO ABOVE\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"- The game is now 20% bigger! (58 new events, 16 new enemies, 30 new items, and 15 new status effects) with three new mysteries and characters to solve them.\n"
"- new location and a new additonal action: MOUNTAINS and METRO\n"
"- two new OLD GODS\n"
"- SCENARIO MODE, revealing the story behind the FOREST TAPES\n"
"- COMBAT CASTING — trade instant effects for increased damage\n"
"- The ability to lock a mystery when rerolling\n"
"- PLANNER — available on the wardrobe screen at home, showing which achievements can be unlocked during your current playthrough\n"
"- WEIRD WEATHER\n"
"- Failed exorcisms now gradually reveal the correct sequence\n"
"- ENDLESS MODE has been slightly reworked, with more exciting rewards\n"
"- New challenges\n"
"- Countless small fixes and balance changes"
msgstr ""
"1.2 AS BELOW SO ABOVE\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"- The game is now 20% bigger! (58 new events, 16 new enemies, 30 new items, and 15 new status effects) with three new mysteries and characters to solve them.\n"
"- new location and a new additonal action: MOUNTAINS and METRO\n"
"- two new OLD GODS\n"
"- SCENARIO MODE, revealing the story behind the FOREST TAPES\n"
"- COMBAT CASTING — trade instant effects for increased damage\n"
"- The ability to lock a mystery when rerolling\n"
"- PLANNER — available on the wardrobe screen at home, showing which achievements can be unlocked during your current playthrough\n"
"- WEIRD WEATHER\n"
"- Failed exorcisms now gradually reveal the correct sequence\n"
"- ENDLESS MODE has been slightly reworked, with more exciting rewards\n"
"- New challenges\n"
"- Countless small fixes and balance changes"

#. Notas de una versión del juego.
msgctxt "woh_ver:1"
msgid ""
"1.0 WELCOME TO SHIOKAWA\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"This update brings WORLD OF HORROR out of the early access stage, major changes including:\n"
"- four new mysteries, bringing new events and enemies\n"
"- two new characters with their own set of new upgrades\n"
"- two new OLD GODS, each bringing new strategies to the game\n"
"- save/load system, take a break without losing any progress\n"
"\n"
"- additional translations of the game, including Japanese, Chinese (traditional), Chinese (simplified), Korean, French and German."
msgstr ""
"1.0 WELCOME TO SHIOKAWA\n"
"---------------------\n"
"\n"
"This update brings WORLD OF HORROR out of the early access stage, major changes including:\n"
"- four new mysteries, bringing new events and enemies\n"
"- two new characters with their own set of new upgrades\n"
"- two new OLD GODS, each bringing new strategies to the game\n"
"- save/load system, take a break without losing any progress\n"
"\n"
"- additional translations of the game, including Japanese, Chinese (traditional), Chinese (simplified), Korean, French and German."

msgctxt "woh_yon:0"
msgid "STUFFED TOY"
msgstr "填充玩偶"

msgctxt "woh_yon:1"
msgid "(use): +1 CURSE removal"
msgstr "（使用）：+1 移除詛咒次數"

msgctxt "woh_yon:2"
msgid "The toy crumbles into dust as you feel blessed."
msgstr "玩偶在你感受到祝福後化為了一片塵埃。"

msgctxt "woh_yon:3"
msgid "FLESHY TOY"
msgstr "血肉玩偶"

msgctxt "woh_yon:4"
msgid ""
"[+5% DOOM]\n"
"[+3 MAX REASON]"
msgstr ""
"[+5% 末日]\n"
"[+3 理智上限]"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:5"
msgid "ROOMMATE"
msgstr "室友"

#. Descripción de «ROOMMATE» (woh_yon:5).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:6"
msgid ""
"The wall opens even further... deeper...\n"
"A girl lies curled up inside of the apartment's womb.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
">>i j u s t want y o u to be safe h e r e<<\n"
">>what d i d i do?<<\n"
">>why won't you j u s t s t a y?<<"
msgstr ""
"牆壁一層一層地打開……\n"
"在牆壁的最深處，你看見一個女孩，而她整個人的身體蜷縮在公寓的子宮內。\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"『我 只 是 希 望 你 在 這 裡 好 好 的』\n"
"\n"
"『我 做 錯 了 什 麼 ？』\n"
"\n"
"『為 什 麼 你 要 離 開 我？』"

#. Parte de «ROOMMATE» (woh_yon:5).
msgctxt "woh_yon:7"
msgid "Sumire-san thought she had everything she wanted. That is, until she met you."
msgstr "堇小姐在遇見你之前，以為自己已經別無所求。是在遇見你之後，她才發現自己缺少了什麼。"

#. Parte de «ROOMMATE» (woh_yon:5).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:8"
msgid ">>stay w i t h me<<"
msgstr "『陪 我 嘛』"

#. Parte de «ROOMMATE» (woh_yon:5).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:9"
msgid ">>p l e a s e don't leave<<"
msgstr "『不 要 走』"

#. Parte de «ROOMMATE» (woh_yon:5).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:10"
msgid ">>I will t a k e care of y o u<<"
msgstr "『我 會 照 顧 你』"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:11"
msgid "RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE"
msgstr "蟄居者綺譚"

#. Descripción de «RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE» (woh_yon:11).
msgctxt "woh_yon:12"
msgid ""
"While you don't get much normalcy in your life these days, today was supposed to be just that.\n"
"\n"
"You'd been planning to take today to de-stress before your next investigation."
msgstr ""
"雖然你最近很少有機會過上正常的生活，但今天本該是那個少數正常的日子才對。\n"
"\n"
"你本來想好要在下一次調查之前，\n"
"利用今天好好放鬆一下。"

#. Parte de «RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE» (woh_yon:11).
msgctxt "woh_yon:13"
msgid ""
"Instead, you awoke to find yourself trapped inside your own apartment. The walls have grown over the door and windows, leaving no exit.\n"
"\n"
"Looking through the peephole, you yell and call out to passing neighbours, but your cries fall on deaf ears."
msgstr ""
"然而，你一覺醒來卻發現你被困在自己的房間裡。原本是門與窗戶的地方長出了牆壁，\n"
"將你徹底關在房間內。\n"
"\n"
"你從貓眼看到鄰居經過時，便開始大聲呼叫求救，但你的叫喊聲卻沒能傳進他們的耳中……"

#. Parte de «RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE» (woh_yon:11).
msgctxt "woh_yon:14"
msgid ""
"Who could have done this to you?\n"
"\n"
"More importantly, how are you going to get out of here?"
msgstr ""
"到底是誰對你做出這種事？\n"
"\n"
"更重要的是，你要怎麼逃離這裡？"

msgctxt "woh_yon:15"
msgid "RESIDENTAL RECLUSE"
msgstr "蟄居者"

msgctxt "woh_yon:16"
msgid "FRONT DOOR"
msgstr "前門"

msgctxt "woh_yon:17"
msgid "PEEPHOLE"
msgstr "貓眼"

msgctxt "woh_yon:18"
msgid "CLOSET"
msgstr "壁櫥"

msgctxt "woh_yon:19"
msgid "KITCHEN"
msgstr "廚房"

msgctxt "woh_yon:20"
msgid "YOUR ROOM"
msgstr "你的房間"

msgctxt "woh_yon:21"
msgid "MAIN ROOM"
msgstr "客廳"

msgctxt "woh_yon:22"
msgid "??"
msgstr "？？"

msgctxt "woh_yon:23"
msgid "PREPARE FOR COMBAT"
msgstr "準備戰鬥"

msgctxt "woh_yon:24"
msgid "SACRIFICE THE TOY"
msgstr "犧牲玩偶"

msgctxt "woh_yon:25"
msgid "WASTE ANOTHER DAY"
msgstr "浪費一整天"

msgctxt "woh_yon:26"
msgid "APPROACH THE WALL"
msgstr "靠近牆壁"

msgctxt "woh_yon:27"
msgid "LOOK THROUGH PEEPHOLE"
msgstr "從貓眼往外看"

msgctxt "woh_yon:28"
msgid "SACRIFICE THE TOY"
msgstr "犧牲玩具"

msgctxt "woh_yon:29"
msgid "LOOK BENEATH SHELVES"
msgstr "查看架子底部"

msgctxt "woh_yon:30"
msgid "CHECK THE NOTE"
msgstr "查看筆記"

msgctxt "woh_yon:31"
msgid "Something guides your hand. What is this?..."
msgstr "有東西引導了你的手。這是什麼……？"

msgctxt "woh_yon:32"
msgid "You don't find anything else."
msgstr "你沒找到其他東西。"

msgctxt "woh_yon:33"
msgid ""
"[[I used to live here too. This was the only place that was saf(...)d good.\n"
"All I could do was stay in, eat and sleep. And when the food ran out, just sleep.]]\n"
"[[When someone eventually came for my corpse, I'd already made my way _inside_.]]\n"
"[[You moved it. I can't tell you how happy being with you has made me. Please don't worry, I will keep you safe. I promise.]]"
msgstr ""
"[[我也曾經住在這裡喔。\n"
"這裡是唯一安全（……）美好的地方。\n"
"我能做的只有待在家、吃飯和睡覺。\n"
"沒有食物之後，就只剩下睡覺。]]\n"
"[[等到有人來找我的屍體時，\n"
"我就已經住在「裡面」了。]]\n"
"[[你接著就住了進來。和你在一起的時候，我真的開心到不知道該怎麼形容才好。\n"
"請別擔心，我會好好保護你的。我發誓。]]"

msgctxt "woh_yon:34"
msgid ""
"...wait, what's that? \n"
"(+ ITEM)"
msgstr "……等等，這是什麼？（+ 物品）"

msgctxt "woh_yon:35"
msgid "You don't have the energy to keep searching."
msgstr "你沒力氣繼續搜索了。"

msgctxt "woh_yon:36"
msgid ""
"You look around but don't find anything. \n"
"(+2% DOOM)"
msgstr ""
"你四處尋找，卻什麼也沒找到。\n"
"（+2% 末日）"

msgctxt "woh_yon:37"
msgid "CHECK BEHIND WARDROBE"
msgstr "查看衣櫃後方"

msgctxt "woh_yon:38"
msgid "CHECK BEHIND BED"
msgstr "查看床後方"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:39"
msgid "CHECK BEHIND DESK"
msgstr "查看書桌後方"

#. Descripción de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:40"
msgid ""
"The windows are covered in a thick layer of drywall, leaving only shallow cavities. The front door isn't much better.\n"
"\n"
"But there must be some way out, right?"
msgstr ""
"窗戶被厚厚的一層石膏板所覆蓋，只留下一些淺淺的小洞。\n"
"前門也被封得死死的。\n"
"\n"
"總會有個出口能讓你逃離吧……？"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:41"
msgid "You spend all of your time searching your apartment for a way out, but you're already getting exhausted."
msgstr "你把所有時間花在尋找公寓的其他出口，但你已經累壞了。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:42"
msgid "Wallpaper and paint have spread around the door's edges. No matter how hard you try, the door refuses to budge."
msgstr "壁紙與油漆已經蔓延到門的邊緣。無論你多用力，門就是打不開。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:43"
msgid "...at least he can't get through, either."
msgstr "……至少他也進不來。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:44"
msgid "Your sleep schedule is starting to drift. The hours just seem to slip past you, and the day is over before you know it."
msgstr ""
"你的睡眠開始變得不規律。\n"
"時間似乎在不知不覺間消逝，而一天就這樣過去了。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:45"
msgid "Wallpaper and paint have spread around the door's edges. No matter how hard you try, the door refuses to budge."
msgstr "壁紙與油漆已經蔓延到門的邊緣。無論你多用力，門就是打不開。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:46"
msgid "There's a weird drawing stuck to your door..."
msgstr "你的門上貼了一張奇怪的畫……"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:47"
msgid ""
"You've read all of your books and watched all of your VHS tapes three times over.\n"
"\n"
"God, you miss people."
msgstr ""
"你已經讀遍了家中所有的書，還把所有的錄影帶都看了整整三遍。\n"
"\n"
"天啊，你真想和其他人交流。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:48"
msgid ""
"You wonder just how much things are changing out there without you around.\n"
"\n"
"If nothing else, you're at least safer in here than out there."
msgstr ""
"你在想，外面的世界沒有你，不知道會有什麼改變。\n"
"\n"
"往好處想，至少待在家裡比待在外面安全多了。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:49"
msgid "You don't see anything of interest in the hallway today."
msgstr "走廊上沒有任何你感興趣的事物。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:50"
msgid "You still change clothes every day, but is there any point if you're not going outside?"
msgstr "你還是會每天換新衣服，但如果沒有要出門的話，這還有意義嗎？"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:51"
msgid "Your pantry is starting to run out of easy meals, and you don't have the energy to cook."
msgstr "你的食品儲藏櫃中快沒有速食了，而你也沒什麼力氣煮飯。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:52"
msgid "You're running out of ways to keep yourself busy. The boredom makes you want to beat your head against a wall."
msgstr "你快沒有事情可做了。你無聊到想拿自己的頭去撞牆。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:53"
msgid ""
"You wonder just how much things are changing out there without you around.\n"
"\n"
"If nothing else, you're at least safer in here than out there."
msgstr ""
"你在想，外面的世界沒有你，不知道會有什麼改變。\n"
"\n"
"往好處想，至少待在家裡比待在外面安全多了。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:54"
msgid "You can't see outside anymore..."
msgstr "你再也看不到外面了……"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:55"
msgid "You still change clothes every day, but is there any point if you're not going outside?"
msgstr "你還是會每天換衣服，但如果沒有要出門的話，這還有意義嗎？"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:56"
msgid "Your pantry is starting to run out of easy meals, and you don't have the energy to cook."
msgstr "你的食品儲藏櫃中快沒有速食了，而你也沒什麼力氣煮飯。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:57"
msgid ""
"Just standing in here makes you light-headed.\n"
"The bed is too tempting-- you shouldn't stay long."
msgstr ""
"光是站在這裡就讓你頭暈。\n"
"床實在是太誘人了，你不該停留過久。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:58"
msgid ""
"Your mind is hazy. It's all blurring together.\n"
"You just want to sleep."
msgstr ""
"你的腦袋一團混亂。\n"
"你只想睡覺。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:59"
msgid ""
"You're beginning to doubt this door will ever open again.\n"
"\n"
"(it's better that way)"
msgstr ""
"你開始懷疑這道門是不是永遠打不開。\n"
"\n"
"（這樣更好）"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:60"
msgid "... what were you doing again?"
msgstr "……忘記自己打算要做什麼了。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:61"
msgid "You don't have much of an appetite."
msgstr "你沒什麼胃口。"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
msgctxt "woh_yon:62"
msgid "(the apartment cradles you gently in your sleep every night, keeping you warm within her ribcage)"
msgstr ""
"（在你每天晚上進入夢鄉時，\n"
"這間公寓都會輕輕地抱著你，讓你沉浸在她溫暖的胸腔中）"

#. Parte de «CHECK BEHIND DESK» (woh_yon:39).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:63"
msgid ""
"As you get closer, you notice thin cracks in the wall above the bed. Something dark, glistening red pulsates inside. The cracks move like lips, and the apartment whispers to you.\n"
">>just lay down<<\n"
"\n"
"You hear wooden support beams creak as the walls flex, reaching toward you from all sides.\n"
">>and let me take care of you<<"
msgstr ""
"你在靠近時，注意到床的牆壁上有道很淺的裂縫。有個閃閃發亮的暗紅色物體正在裡頭緩緩跳動著。這間公寓透過那像是嘴唇的裂縫，對你輕聲說道。\n"
"『躺下來』\n"
"房間的木樑接著開始發出嘎吱嘎吱的聲音，\n"
"牆壁也從四面八方彎曲，朝你靠了過來。\n"
"『讓我來好好照顧你』"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:64"
msgid "MYSTERY MEAT"
msgstr "神秘肉塊"

#. Descripción de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64).
msgctxt "woh_yon:65"
msgid ""
"No access to the outside world means you only have so much food to eat.\n"
"\n"
"Deep in the back of your pantry, you discover a rusty can of meat. How long this has this thing been in here? \n"
"\n"
"Opening the can, it smells fine, but..."
msgstr ""
"無法與外界交流，表示你有一天食物會吃完。\n"
"\n"
"你在食品儲藏櫃的深處，發現了一罐生鏽的肉罐頭。\n"
"這東西在這裡面放多久了？\n"
"\n"
"你把罐頭打開後，沒有聞到什麼異味，但……"

#. Opción de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64). Opciones: eat it · throw it away.
msgctxt "woh_yon:66"
msgid "eat it"
msgstr "吃掉"

#. Opción de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64). Opciones: eat it · throw it away.
msgctxt "woh_yon:67"
msgid "throw it away"
msgstr "丟掉"

#. Parte de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64).
msgctxt "woh_yon:68"
msgid ""
"It's not exactly a pleasant meal - meat definitely shouldn't be this crunchy - but food is food.\n"
"(+2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"這塊肉的口感為什麼會那麼酥脆……？\n"
"你開始懷疑自己究竟是吃下了什麼東西，\n"
"但能吃飽就好了，不要太強求。\n"
"（+2 體力）"

#. Parte de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64).
msgctxt "woh_yon:69"
msgid ""
"You already regret your decision by the first disgusting bite. \n"
"\n"
"An hour later, you feel something writhing in your stomach, trying to get out. Maybe that meat was too fresh...\n"
"(+ STATUS)"
msgstr ""
"你才剛咬下那塊肉，\n"
"你就後悔自己決定要吃下這噁心的東西。\n"
"\n"
"一小時過後，你覺得有東西在你的胃裡翻攪著，試著想要逃出去。那塊肉似乎太「生」了……\n"
"（+ 狀態）"

#. Parte de «MYSTERY MEAT» (woh_yon:64).
msgctxt "woh_yon:70"
msgid ""
"Trusting your judgement, you chuck the can into the garbage. Your stomach growls at you in discontentment.\n"
"(-1 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"你相信自己的判斷，把罐頭丟進了垃圾桶。\n"
"你的肚子咕嚕咕嚕叫個不停，好像在對你抗議一樣。\n"
"（-1 體力）"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:71"
msgid "CLOGGED DRAIN"
msgstr "堵塞的排水口"

#. Descripción de «CLOGGED DRAIN» (woh_yon:71).
msgctxt "woh_yon:72"
msgid ""
"When you go to use the bathroom, you notice there's a clump of hair coming up the sink drain. \n"
"\n"
"You're certain that it's not yours."
msgstr ""
"你去上廁所時，發現洗手台的排水口冒出了一團頭髮。\n"
"\n"
"你很確定那不是你的頭髮。"

#. Opción de «CLOGGED DRAIN» (woh_yon:71). Opciones: pull it out.
msgctxt "woh_yon:73"
msgid "pull it out"
msgstr "把頭髮拉出來"

#. Parte de «CLOGGED DRAIN» (woh_yon:71).
msgctxt "woh_yon:74"
msgid ""
"You tug the strand up out of the drain, only to find a few coins tied to the end of the hair. You pocket the money and try not to think about it.\n"
"(+1 FUNDS)"
msgstr ""
"你將這撮頭髮從排水口給硬扯出來，結果發現頭髮末端居然綁著幾枚硬幣。你把錢放進口袋，試著想把整件事拋在腦後。\n"
"（+1 金錢）"

#. Parte de «CLOGGED DRAIN» (woh_yon:71).
msgctxt "woh_yon:75"
msgid ""
"There's a startling amount of resistance when you pull. Before you can react, the hair is suddenly yanked back down the drain and out of sight.\n"
"(-1 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"才正要拉出頭髮，你就感受到一股驚人的力道在抵抗。在你能反應前，那撮頭髮就被扯回了排水口內，不留下任何痕跡。\n"
"（-1 理智）"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:76"
msgid "KILLING TIME"
msgstr "殺時間"

#. Descripción de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76).
msgctxt "woh_yon:77"
msgid ""
"Sitting on the sofa, you find yourself repeatedly checking the time to get some grounding.\n"
"\n"
"When you go to eat, though, you realize the clock in the kitchen displays a different time. And your bedroom alarm clock is completely different from each of the others."
msgstr ""
"坐在沙發上的時候，你會一直確認時間，想藉此讓自己冷靜下來。\n"
"\n"
"然而，當你去廚房吃飯時，卻發現那邊的時鐘顯示的時間和客廳的不一樣。就連臥室的鬧鐘，也顯示著不一樣的時間。"

#. Opción de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76). Opciones: <<they need a battery change, probably>> · <<I must be delirious>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:78"
msgid "<<they need a battery change, probably>>"
msgstr "「大概是電池快沒電了吧」"

#. Opción de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76). Opciones: <<they need a battery change, probably>> · <<I must be delirious>>.
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:79"
msgid "<<I must be delirious>>"
msgstr "「我一定是開始精神錯亂了」"

#. Parte de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76).
msgctxt "woh_yon:80"
msgid ""
"You're sure there's some explanation. You shrug it off and get your food.\n"
"\n"
"You pretend you're not nauseous when the clocks later show negative numbers, jumbled words, and nothing at all.\n"
"(+1 STAMINA / -2 REASON)"
msgstr ""
"這一定有什麼合理的解釋。\n"
"你決定不去想那麼多，回頭拿你的食物。\n"
"\n"
"在這之後，時鐘上開始顯示負數、亂碼，或是什麼都沒顯示。你看到之後還逞強，假裝自己沒有覺得頭暈想吐。\n"
"（+1 體力/-2 理智）"

#. Parte de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76).
msgctxt "woh_yon:81"
msgid ""
"Being stuck in here is really starting to get to your head. To set yourself straight, you slap yourself hard enough to see stars, chug some coffee, and avoid looking at the clocks again.\n"
"(+1 REASON / -2 STAMINA)"
msgstr ""
"長期困在家裡，真的會對你的身心造成影響。為了讓自己振作，你狠狠打了自己一巴掌，再灌了一杯咖啡，然後盡量不要讓自己看到時鐘。\n"
"（+1 理智/-2 體力）"

#. Parte de «KILLING TIME» (woh_yon:76).
msgctxt "woh_yon:82"
msgid "WASTING ANOTHER DAY..."
msgstr "浪費一整天……"

msgctxt "woh_yon:83"
msgid "A - FINALLY FREE"
msgstr "A - 回歸自由的懷抱"

#. Título; los textos siguientes forman parte de su bloque.
msgctxt "woh_yon:84"
msgid "B - EVIL EVICTED"
msgstr "B - 驅散邪惡"

#. Descripción de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:85"
msgid ""
"The girl's face twists oddly. The apartment's pulsing innards slow to a still.\n"
"\n"
"The girl mouths something you can't make out. She smiles. You fall unconscious.\n"
"\n"
"When you awaken, you're laying in the apartment entryway, beside the open door."
msgstr ""
"女孩的容貌開始扭曲變形，\n"
"公寓的內臟也漸漸沒了脈搏。\n"
"\n"
"她在張口說出一些你聽不懂的話之後，\n"
"對你露出了一抹微笑。在這之後，你便失去了意識。\n"
"\n"
"再次睜開眼時，你發現自己正躺在公寓的玄關，\n"
"而旁邊的門是開著的。"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:86"
msgid ""
"The next morning, you see a silhouette on the balcony, staring out at Shiokawa and watching the sunrise.\n"
"You blink, and she's gone."
msgstr ""
"隔天清晨，你看見有道人影站在陽台上，\n"
"看著太陽緩緩從鹽川的地平線升起。\n"
"你眨眼後，她就消失了。"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:87"
msgid ""
"After that, you never see her again, and after that, your apartment becomes just an apartment.\n"
"\n"
"[RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE:\n"
"ENDING A]"
msgstr ""
"在那之後，你就再也沒見過她。\n"
"從此之後，你的公寓也恢復了正常。\n"
"\n"
"[蟄居者綺譚：結局 A]"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:88"
msgid ""
"An expression of agony overtakes the girl's face. Her hair gets tangled into the apartment's churning guts, and her flesh begins to melt apart.\n"
"She arches her back in a voiceless scream until her pale body finally collapses in on itself."
msgstr ""
"女孩臉上的表情顯得很痛苦。她的頭髮與公寓翻騰的腸胃糾纏在一起，她的血肉也開始溶解。\n"
"她拱起背，發出無聲的尖叫，直到她蒼白的屍體倒下為止。"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:89"
msgid ""
"When you stumble out of the room, things seem to have returned to normal, and your door can open again. Relieved, you take the chance to go out for a walk.\n"
"Only a few hours later do you return to the bedroom, and find a lump beneath your bed's covers."
msgstr ""
"在你一拐一拐地走出房間後，一切似乎都恢復正常，你的門又能再度開啟了。你鬆了一口氣，趁機出門走走。\n"
"幾小時後，你回到臥室，卻發現床罩下有顆腫塊。"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
msgctxt "woh_yon:90"
msgid "Peeling back the sheets reveals the toy that you had destroyed, the pieces held together with sections of pulsing flesh. Beside its body is a small note."
msgstr ""
"你掀開床罩，發現之前被你破壞掉的玩偶。\n"
"它的各個部分，被帶著脈搏的血肉給重新組起。\n"
"你在它身體旁邊看到一張小紙條。"

#. Parte de «B - EVIL EVICTED» (woh_yon:84).
#. Diálogo o pensamiento entre << >>.
msgctxt "woh_yon:91"
msgid ""
">>i'll\n"
"a l w a y s\n"
"keep you safe<<\n"
"\n"
"[RESTLESS RUMORS OF A RESIDENTIAL RECLUSE:\n"
"ENDING B]"
msgstr ""
"『我會\n"
"永 遠 永 遠 永 遠\n"
"在你身邊保護你的』\n"
"\n"
"[蟄居者綺譚：結局 B]"
